hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"601","601 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hudayj ibn Mu'awiya narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'd ibn Iyas, from a man who married a woman from Banu Shamkh, then he saw her mother afterwards and she pleased him, so he went to Ibn Mas'ud and said: I married a woman and did not consummate with her, then her mother pleased me, so shall I divorce the woman and marry her mother? He said: Yes. So he divorced her and married her mother. Then Abdillah went to Madina and asked the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they said: It is not lawful. Then he came back and went to Banu Shamkh and said: Where is the man who married the mother of the woman who was under him? They said: Here he is. He said: Let him separate from her. They said: And she has borne him children? He said: Let him separate from her, for she is forbidden by Allah, mighty and majestic."
"602","602 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Mughira narrated, from Ibrahim, from Shurayh, that he was asked about that, and he said: Go to Banu Shamkh and ask them."
"603","603 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated, he said: I asked Ibn Abi Najih about a man who married a woman and divorced her before consummating with her, until she died, or he divorced her: may his son marry her? He said: concerning it Dawud killed his son, I judge. [Flag: phrasing in source is garbled/truncated]"
"604","604 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, that he was asked about 'and your wives' mothers.' He said: It is unqualified; leave general what Allah left general and follow what Allah made clear; and he permitted the stepdaughter if he had not entered her mother, and he disliked the mother in every case."
"605","His saying, exalted: 'And married women except what your right hands possess.' 605 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu Mu'awiya narrated, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Abdillah, concerning His saying, exalted: 'And married women except what your right hands possess' - he said: Every married woman is forbidden to you unless you buy her or what your right hand possesses."
"606","606 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from al-Salt ibn Bahram, from Ibrahim, concerning His statement, mighty and majestic: 'And married women except what your right hands possess' - he said: Except the captives from the people of war."
"607","607 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu Mu'awiya narrated, from al-A'mash, from Yahya ibn Waththab, that he used to recite this verse: 'And married women except what your right hands possess.'"
"608","608 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu Awana narrated, from Ismail ibn Salim, from al-Sha'bi, concerning His statement, mighty and majestic: 'And married women except what your right hands possess' - he said: The chastity of the slave girl is her entering Islam and affirming it; when she enters Islam and affirms it, then commits adultery, upon her is fifty lashes."
"609","609 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Mutarrif narrated, from al-Sha'bi, concerning His statement, mighty and majestic: 'And the chaste from those given the Book before you' - he said: Her chastity is that she guards her private part from fornication and washes from major impurity."
"610","610 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from Abu Umayya and Humayd, from Mujahid, he said: He used to recite everything in the Quran as 'muhsinat' except the one in al-Nisa: 'And married women.'"
"611","611 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Attab ibn Bashir narrated, from Khusayf, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, concerning His statement, mighty and majestic: 'And the chaste' - he said: The chaste, sane woman, whether Muslim or from the People of the Book."
"612","His saying, exalted: 'And whoever among you cannot afford to marry the believing chaste women, then from what your right hands possess of your believing girls' to His saying: 'that is for whoever fears hardship among you, and that you be patient is better for you, and Allah is Forgiving, Merciful.' 612 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Mughira narrated, from Ibrahim, that he used to recite: 'then when they are chaste'; he said: when they enter Islam; and Mujahid used to recite: 'then when they are chaste,' saying: when they marry; so long as she has not married there is no hadd upon her."
"613","613 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated, from Ikrima - or another, Dawud doubted - from Ibn Abbas, that he did not see any hadd upon the slave girl until she marries a free husband."
"614","614 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated, he said: Thumama ibn Abdillah ibn Anas narrated to me, he said: I witnessed Anas ibn Malik flogging his slave girls the hadd when they fornicated, whether they had married or not."
"615","615 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Mujahid, he said: Ibn Abbas said: There is no hadd upon the slave girl until she becomes chaste."
"616","616 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from Mis'ar, from Amr ibn Murra, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that he used to say: There is no hadd upon the slave girl until she becomes chaste, because Allah says: 'then when they are chaste, if they commit indecency.'"
"617","617 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Abu Bishr narrated, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, concerning His statement, mighty and majestic: 'And whoever among you cannot afford to marry the believing chaste women, then from what your right hands possess' - he said: Means is wealth; when he does not find what to marry a free woman with, he marries a slave girl."
"618","618 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Abu Bishr told me, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: The marrier of slave girls has barely kept away from adultery; 'and that you be patient is better for you' - he said: from marrying slave girls."
"619","619 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, he said: The marriage of the slave girls of the People of the Book is not lawful, because Allah, mighty and majestic, says: 'of your believing girls.'"
"620","620 - Sa'id narrated, Hushaym narrated, he said: al-Awwam narrated, from one who narrated to him, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The marrier of slave girls has barely moved away from adultery."
"621","621 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, and Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak, that they both said: Hardship means adultery."
"622","His saying, exalted: 'O you who believe, do not consume your wealth among you in falsehood except it be trade by mutual consent among you, and do not kill yourselves; indeed Allah is Merciful to you. And whoever does that in aggression and wrong, We shall roast him in Fire, and that is easy for Allah.' 622 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Asim ibn Bahdala, that Masruq came to Siffin and stood between the two ranks and said: O people, listen: what if a caller called you from heaven and you saw him and heard his speech, saying: Allah forbids you what you are in - would you desist? He said: So they reviled him. He said: By Allah, Jibril, peace be upon him, came down with that, and that is with us no clearer than Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); indeed Allah says: 'O you who believe, do not consume...' He said: Then he entered among the people and returned to Kufa."
"623","His saying, exalted: 'And do not wish for what Allah favored some of you with over others; for men a share of what they earned, and for women a share of what they earned; and ask Allah of His bounty; indeed Allah is Knowing of everything.' 623 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Attab ibn Bashir narrated, he said: Khusayf narrated, from Ikrima, concerning His statement, mighty and majestic: 'And do not wish...' - he claimed that the women asked for jihad, saying: We wish Allah, mighty and majestic, had made fighting for us so we would gain of the reward what men gain; so Allah revealed: 'And do not wish for what Allah favored...'"
"624","624 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, he said: Umm Salama said: Men fight and we do not fight, and we have only half the inheritance; so 'And do not wish for what Allah favored some of you with over others' was revealed to the end of the verse, and 'Indeed the Muslim men and Muslim women, and the believing men and believing women' was revealed to the end of the verse."
"625","His saying, exalted: 'And those whom your oaths bound, give them their share.' 625 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: A man would covenant with a man, and each of them would inherit the other; and Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, covenanted with a man and inherited him."
"626","626 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, concerning His statement, mighty and majestic: 'And for all We made heirs of what the parents and relatives left' - he said: The agnates; 'And those whom your oaths bound, give them their share' - he said: The allies; 'give them their share' - he said: of blood-money, aid, and support."
"627","627 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, that he used to recite: 'your oaths covenanted.'"
"628","His saying, exalted: 'And if you fear dissension between them, send an arbiter from his family and an arbiter from her family; if they both desire reform, Allah will bring agreement between them; indeed Allah is Knowing, Aware.' 628 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abida al-Salmani, he said: A man and a woman came to Ali, with a crowd of people with them; so Ali sent an arbiter from her family and an arbiter from his family, then he said to the two arbiters: Do you know what is upon you? If you see separation, you separate them, and if you see union, you unite them. The woman said: I accept the words of Allah for me and against me. The husband said: As for separation, no. So Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: No, by Allah, until you affirm as she affirmed."
"629","629 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated, Mansur and Hisham narrated, from Ibn Sirin, from Abida, like it: The woman said: I accept and submit. The husband said: As for separation, no. So Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: That is not yours; you shall not leave until you accept as she accepted."
"630","630 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Husayn narrated, from al-Sha'bi, that a woman was recalcitrant toward her husband, so they disputed to Shurayh; Shurayh said: Send an arbiter from his family and an arbiter from her family. They did so; the two arbiters looked into their matter and saw fit to separate them, but the man disliked that; so Shurayh said: Then in what were we today? And he upheld their decision."
"631","631 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated, he said: I heard al-Sha'bi saying: Whatever the two arbiters judge is valid, whether they separate or unite."
"632","632 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated, from Ubayda, from Ibrahim, like that."
"633","633 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated, from Shu'ba, from Amr ibn Murra, he said: I asked Sa'id ibn Jubayr about the two arbiters, and he became angry and said: I was not even born then. I said: I mean only the arbitration of dissension. He said: When there is repelling or contention between the man and the woman, they send two arbiters; they turn to the one from whose side the contention is, admonish him and command him; if he obeys them, well, otherwise they turn to the other; if he hears them and comes to what they want, well, otherwise they judge between them; and whatever they judge is valid. Shu'ba said: And most of my knowledge is that a man beside me said to me: it is valid."
"634","His saying, exalted: 'And the companion at the side.' 634 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abdillah ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Muhammad ibn Suqa, from Ibrahim, concerning His statement, mighty and majestic: 'And the companion at the side' - he said: The wife."
"635","His saying, exalted: 'Who are miserly and command people with miserliness.' 635 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, he heard Ubayd ibn Umayr reciting: 'and command people with miserliness.'"
"636","His saying, exalted: 'Indeed Allah does not wrong a mote's weight; and if it be a good deed He multiplies it and gives from Himself a great reward.' 636 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from Fudayl ibn Marzuq, from Atiyya al-Awfi, from Ibn Umar, concerning His statement, mighty and majestic: 'Whoever comes with a good deed has ten like it' - he said: This is for the people of the desert; so what is for the people of the towns? He said: 'and if it be a good deed He multiplies it and gives from Himself a great reward'; and when Allah says of a thing 'great,' it is great."
"637","His saying, exalted: 'O you who believe, do not approach prayer while intoxicated until you know what you say, nor in major impurity except passers through until you wash; and if you are ill or on a journey or one of you came from the privy or you touched women and find no water, then seek clean earth and wipe your faces and hands; indeed Allah is Pardoning, Forgiving.' 637 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated, from Sa'id ibn Abi Aruba, from Qatada, he said: We said to Sa'id ibn Jubayr, concerning His statement: 'and if you are ill or on a journey...' I said: What is the concession of the sick here? He said: When he has sores, wounds, or water is hard upon him, he performs tayammum with earth."
"638","638 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Khalid ibn Abdillah narrated, from Bayan, from Amir al-Sha'bi, from Abdillah, he said: Touching is what is less than intercourse, and the kiss is of it, and from it is wudu."
"639","639 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Abu Ubayda, from Abdillah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The kiss is of touching, and from it is wudu."
"640","640 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu Awana narrated, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: We were in the room of Ibn Abbas, with us Ata ibn Abi Rabah and a group of the mawali, and Ubayd ibn Umayr and a group of the Arabs; we discussed touching. I and Ata said: Touching is with the hand. Ubayd ibn Umayr and the Arabs said: It is intercourse. I said: You have near you of this merit close by; so I entered upon Ibn Abbas while he was sitting on a bed, and he said to me: What is it? I said: We discussed touching; some of us said it is touching with the hand, and some said it is intercourse. He said: Who said it is intercourse? I said: The Arabs. He said: And who said it is touching with the hand? I said: The mawali. He said: From which of the two parties were you? I said: With the mawali. He laughed and said: The mawali prevailed, the mawali prevailed - three times - then he said: Touching, feeling, and embracing short of intercourse is not it; but Allah, mighty and majestic, alludes to what He wills with what He wills."
"641","641 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Abu Bishr narrated, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Touching, feeling, and embracing short of intercourse is not it; but Allah, mighty and majestic, alluded to it."
"642","642 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated, from Mughira, from Ibrahim, that he used to recite: 'or you touched women.' He said: meaning what is less than intercourse."
"643","643 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated, he said: Salama ibn Alqama narrated, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, he said: I asked Abida about His statement: 'or you touched women,' and he gestured with his hand, and I understood what he said. [Flag: gesture undescribed in source; rendered literally]"
"644","644 - And Muhammad said: And I was told from Ibn Umar that when he touched his private part he performed wudu; so I thought the statement of Ibn Umar and Abida is one thing."
"645","645 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Abu al-Zubayr narrated, from Jabir, he said: One of us would pass through the mosque in major impurity, merely passing."
"646","646 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated, from Hisham ibn Sa'd, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, he said: I saw men from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sitting in the mosque while in major impurity, when they had performed the wudu of prayer."
"647","647 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated, from Hisham ibn Sa'd, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, he said: The Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would enter the mosque and leave it and not pray in it; and I saw Ibn Umar doing it."
"648","His saying, exalted: 'Have you not seen those given a share of the Book believing in jibt and taghut, and saying to those who disbelieved: These are better guided than those who believed, in way. Those are whom Allah cursed, and whom Allah curses you will never find for him a helper.' 648 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrima, he said: Huyayy ibn Akhtab and Ka'b ibn al-Ashraf came to Makka, and Quraysh said: You are people of the Book and knowledge: are we better or Muhammad? They said: What are you, and what is Muhammad? They said: A rootless one who cut our kinship, and the thieves of the pilgrims, Banu Ghifar, followed him; so are we better guided in way or he? They said: You are. So Allah revealed: 'Have you not seen those given a share of the Book...'"
"649","649 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Hassan al-Absi, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Jibt is sorcery, and taghut is Satan; and courage and cowardice are instincts in men: the brave fights for one he does not know, and the coward flees from his father; and a man's nobility is his religion, and his lineage is his character, even if he be Persian or Nabataean."
"650","His saying, exalted: 'Or have they a share of dominion? Then they would not give people a naqir.' 650 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated, from Khusayf, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The naqir is the notch in the side of the date-stone, and the qitmir is the skin upon the date-stone."
"651","His saying, exalted: 'Indeed Allah commands you to render trusts to their owners, and when you judge between people to judge with justice; indeed excellent is what Allah admonishes you with; indeed Allah is Hearing, Seeing. O you who believe, obey Allah and obey the Messenger and those in authority among you; and if you dispute in anything, refer it to Allah and the Messenger, if you believe in Allah and the Last Day; that is better and best in outcome.' 651 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Marwan ibn Mu'awiya narrated, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated, he said: Mus'ab ibn Sa'd narrated, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, spoke words in which he was right: It is incumbent upon the imam to judge by what Allah, mighty and majestic, sent down, and to render the trust; and when he does that, it is incumbent upon the people to listen to him, obey him, and answer when called."
"652","652 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu Mu'awiya narrated, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, concerning His statement: 'obey Allah and obey the Messenger and those in authority among you' - he said: They are the rulers."
"653","653 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu Mu'awiya narrated, from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, he said: They are the jurists and scholars."
"654","654 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Mansur narrated, from al-Hasan. [Flag: report text truncated in source; rendered literally]"
"655","655 - And Abd al-Malik told us, from Ata, they both said: Those of understanding and knowledge. [Flag: isnad start truncated in source]"
"656","656 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Ismail ibn Zakariya narrated, from Layth, from Mujahid, he said: Those of understanding and knowledge; 'and if you dispute in anything, refer it to Allah and the Messenger' - he said: to the Book of Allah, and 'to the Messenger' - he said: to the Sunna of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); then he recited: 'and if they had referred it to the Messenger and to those in authority among them, those who derive it among them would have known it.'"
"657","657 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from al-Hakam ibn Aban, he said: Ikrima was asked about the mothers of children, and he said: They are free. It was said to him: By what do you say it? He said: By the Quran. They said: By what of the Quran? He said: The saying of Allah: 'obey Allah and obey the Messenger and those in authority among you'; and Umar was of those in authority; he said: She is freed even if it be a miscarriage."
"658","658 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu Awana narrated, from Mughira, from al-Sha'bi, from Abida, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, addressed the people and said: Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, consulted me concerning the mothers of children, and I and Umar saw fit to free them; so Umar judged by it in his lifetime, and Uthman in his lifetime; then when I took charge I saw fit to enslave them. Abida said: The view of Umar and Ali together is dearer to me than the view of Ali alone."
"659","His saying, exalted: 'And if, when they wronged themselves, they had come to you and asked forgiveness of Allah, and the Messenger had asked forgiveness for them, they would have found Allah Relenting, Merciful.' 659 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from Mis'ar, from Ma'n ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, he said: Abdillah said: In al-Nisa there are five verses I would not exchange for the world and what is in it, and I know that the scholars when they pass them know them: 'If you avoid the major sins of what you are forbidden, We shall expiate your evil deeds and admit you a noble entrance,' and His saying: 'Indeed Allah does not wrong a mote's weight...,' and: 'Indeed Allah does not forgive that partners be associated with Him and forgives less than that for whom He wills,' the verse, 'And if, when they wronged themselves, they had come to you...,' 'And whoever does evil or wrongs himself then seeks Allah's forgiveness will find Allah Forgiving, Merciful.'"
"660","His saying, exalted: 'But no, by your Lord, they will not believe until they make you judge in what disputes between them, then find in themselves no discomfort from what you decided, and submit in submission.' 660 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Salama of the descendants of Umm Salama, he said: A man disputed with al-Zubayr to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged for al-Zubayr; he said: He judged for him only because he is his aunt's son; so 'But no, by your Lord, they will not believe...' was revealed."
"661","His saying, exalted: 'And whoever obeys Allah and the Messenger, those are with those Allah favored of the prophets, the truthful, and the martyrs' to His saying 'and sufficient is Allah as Knower.' 661 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Khalaf ibn Khalifa narrated, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from al-Sha'bi, he said: A man from the Ansar came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: You are dearer to me than myself, my child, my family, and my wealth; and were I not to come to you and see you, I would think I shall die; and the Ansari wept. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What made you weep? He said: I remembered that you will die and we shall die, so you will be raised with the prophets, and we, when we enter Paradise, shall be below you. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not tell him anything; so Allah revealed upon His Messenger: 'And whoever obeys Allah and the Messenger...' to His saying 'Knower'; so he said: Rejoice."
"662","His saying, exalted: 'Whatever good befalls you is from Allah, and whatever evil befalls you is from yourself; and We sent you to people as a messenger, and sufficient is Allah as witness.' 662 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Abu Salih, concerning His saying: 'and whatever evil befalls you is from yourself' - he said: By your sin, and We decreed it upon you."
"663","His saying, exalted: 'Then what is with you that you are two parties concerning the hypocrites, while Allah cast them back for what they earned?' 663 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Sa'd ibn Mu'adh, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed the people and said: Who will deal for me with one who harms me and gathers in his house one who harms me? Sa'd ibn Mu'adh said: If he is from al-Aws we shall kill him, and if he is from our brothers of al-Khazraj, command us and we shall obey you. Sa'd ibn Ubada stood and said: What is with you, O Ibn Mu'adh, the obedience of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? You have spoken what is not of you. Usayd ibn Hudayr stood and said: You, O Ibn Ubada, are a hypocrite and you love the hypocrites. Muhammad ibn Maslama stood and said: Be silent, O people, for among us is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he commands us and we carry out his command. So Allah revealed: 'Then what is with you that you are two parties concerning the hypocrites...'"
"664","His saying, exalted: 'And it is not for a believer to kill a believer except by mistake; and whoever kills a believer by mistake, then freeing a believing neck and blood-money delivered to his family unless they remit it; and if he was from a people hostile to you and he is a believer, then freeing a believing neck; and if he was from a people between you and them a covenant, then blood-money delivered to his family and freeing a believing neck; and whoever does not find, then fasting two consecutive months, repentance from Allah; and Allah is Knowing, Wise.' 664 - Sa'id narrated, Jarir narrated, from Mughira, from Ibrahim, concerning His statement: 'And it is not for a believer to kill a believer except by mistake...' He said: This is the Muslim whose heirs are the Muslims; 'and if he was from a people hostile to you and he is a believer, then freeing a believing neck' - he said: This is the Muslim man whose people are idolaters, with no covenant between them and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); 'and if he was from a people between you and them a covenant...' - he said: This is the Muslim man whose people are idolaters, with a covenant between them and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he is killed; his inheritance is for the Muslims, and his blood-money is for his people, because they pay blood-money for him."
"665","665 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, from Hajjaj, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah and Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, they both said concerning His saying: 'hostile to you and he is a believer' - they said: A man from the enemy who becomes Muslim and wants to join the Muslims but is killed by mistake; they said: There is no blood-money for him, and upon him is freeing a neck."
"666","His saying, exalted: 'And whoever kills a believer intentionally, his recompense is Hell, abiding in it, and Allah is angry with him, curses him, and prepares for him a great punishment.' 666 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from Ammar al-Duhni and Yahya al-Jabir, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, he said: A man asked Ibn Abbas: What do you say of a man who killed a believing man intentionally, then repented, believed, did righteous deeds, then was guided? He said: And how for him guidance, may his mother be bereaved of him; I heard your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The slain shall come on the Day of Resurrection with his head hanging, his jugular veins gushing blood, saying: O Lord, ask this one: why did he kill me? By Allah, nothing abrogated it after it was revealed: 'And whoever kills a believer intentionally...'"
"667","667 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from Abu al-Zinad, he said: I heard a shaykh saying to Kharija ibn Zayd: I heard your father here saying: The severe verse was revealed, and the light one in al-Furqan: 'and they do not kill the soul Allah forbade except by right, nor fornicate' to His saying 'except whoever repents.'"
"668","668 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Kurdum, that Abu Hurayra, Ibn Abbas, and Ibn Umar were asked about a man who kills a believer intentionally, and they said: Can he avoid dying? Can he seek a tunnel in the earth or a ladder in the heaven, or bring him back to life?"
"669","669 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hammad ibn Yahya al-Abahh narrated, he said: Sa'id ibn Mina narrated, from Abu Hurayra, he said: I was sitting beside him when a man came and said: O Abu Hurayra, what do you say of the killer of a believer, is there repentance for him? He said: No; by the One there is no god but He, he shall not enter Paradise until the camel passes through the eye of the needle."
"670","670 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hammad ibn Yahya al-Abahh narrated, he said: Sa'id ibn Mina narrated, he said: There was a quarrel between a companion of mine and a man of the market people in Makka; my companion took a chair and struck the man's head with it and killed him, and he regretted, saying: I shall give out of my wealth, then go and make myself confined in the way of Allah, mighty and majestic. He said: I said: Let us go to Ibn Umar and ask him: is there repentance for you? So we went until we entered upon him while he was that day in Makka. He said: I said to him: O Abu Abd al-Rahman... and I related the story to him as it was. He said: I said: Do you see any repentance for him? He said: Eat and drink; ugh; get up from me; he claims he did not intend to kill him. He said: He lied; one of you deliberately takes a piece of wood and strikes the head of a Muslim man, then says: I did not intend to kill him. He lied; eat and drink as you can; ugh; get up from me. He added nothing to that until we stood up."
"671","671 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated, he said: al-Awwam ibn Hawshab narrated, he said: I was told from Ibn Mas'ud that he used to say: Killing a believer is a grave barrier."
"672","672 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hammad ibn Yahya narrated, from Abbad al-Minqari, from al-Hasan, he said: By Allah, if the people of the earth and the people of heaven conspired to kill a believer, Allah would admit them all to the Fire."
"673","673 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated, from Ya'la ibn Ata, from his father, from Abdillah ibn Amr, he said: The passing of the whole world is lighter upon Allah, exalted, than the blood of a Muslim shed without right."
"674","674 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Khalid ibn Abdillah narrated, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Abu Mijlaz, concerning His statement: 'then his recompense is Hell' - he said: His recompense is Hell, and if He wills He forgives him."
"675","675 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Kurdum, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man came to him and said: I filled my cistern awaiting my thirsty camels to come to me, and I woke only to a man who had let his she-camel into it, broken the cistern, and spilled the water; so I stood up in fright and struck him with the sword and killed him? He said: This is not like what he said; so he commanded him with repentance. Sufyan said: The people of knowledge, when asked, would say: There is no repentance for him; but when a man was afflicted, they would say to him: Repent."
"676","676 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Jarir narrated, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, he said: Abdillah said: A man remains in ease in his religion so long as he does not shed forbidden blood; and when he sheds forbidden blood, modesty is stripped from him."
"677","His saying, exalted: 'O you who believe, when you go forth in the way of Allah, verify, and do not say to one who offers you peace: You are not a believer, seeking the goods of worldly life.' 677 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Muslims caught up with a man with a small flock of sheep; he said: Peace be upon you; so they killed him and took his flock; then 'and do not say to one who offers you peace: You are not a believer' was revealed."
"678","678 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from Humayd al-A'raj, from Mujahid, that he used to recite 'who offers you peace.'"
"679","679 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Asbahani, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, that he used to recite: 'who offers you peace.'"
"680","680 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Mughira narrated, from Ibrahim, and Awf, from al-Hasan, that they both used to recite: 'who offers you submission.'"
"681","His saying, exalted: 'Not equal are those of the believers who sit, other than those of harm, and those who strive in the way of Allah with their wealth and selves; Allah favored the strivers with their wealth and selves over those who sit by a degree; and to each Allah promised good; and Allah favored the strivers over those who sit with a great reward.' 681 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated, from his father, from Kharija ibn Zayd, that his father Zayd ibn Thabit said: I was beside the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and tranquility came upon him, and the thigh of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell upon my thigh, and I never found anything heavier than the thigh of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); then it was lifted from him and he said: Write. So I wrote on a shoulder-blade: 'Not equal are those of the believers who sit, and those who strive in the way of Allah' to the end of the verse. Then Ibn Umm Maktum stood - and he was a blind man - and when he heard the virtue of the strivers, he said: O Messenger of Allah, what of the believers who cannot strive? Kharija said: Zayd said: When Ibn Umm Maktum finished his speech, tranquility came upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and his thigh fell upon my thigh, and I found of its weight the second time as I found the first time; then it was lifted from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Read, O Zayd. So I recited: 'Not equal are those of the believers who sit.' The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'other than those of harm' - the whole verse. He said: Zayd says: Allah sent it down alone, so I joined it. [Flag: source truncated at end]"
"682","682 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Khalid ibn Abdillah narrated, from Husayn, from Abdillah ibn Shaddad, he said: When this verse was revealed: 'Not equal are those of the believers who sit,' Ibn Umm Maktum stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, indeed in me is what you see; so Allah revealed: 'other than those of harm.'"
"683","683 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas ibn Malik, that he saw Ibn Umm Maktum in one of the Muslims' battlefields with the banner of the Muslims with him."
"684","His saying, exalted: 'And whoever emigrates in the way of Allah will find in the earth many a refuge and abundance.' 684 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, saying concerning His saying: 'will find in the earth many a refuge and abundance' - he said: A removal."
"685","His saying, exalted: 'And whoever leaves his house emigrating to Allah and His Messenger, then death overtakes him, his reward has fallen upon Allah; and Allah is Forgiving, Merciful.' 685 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, that a man from Khuza'a in Makka fell ill - and he is Damra ibn al-Is, or al-Is ibn Damra ibn Zimba - so he ordered his family, and they spread for him upon a bed, carried him, and set out with him heading to Madina; and when he was at al-Tan'im he died; so 'And whoever leaves his house emigrating...' was revealed."
"686","686 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Jarir narrated, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Abu Ayyash al-Zuraqi, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Usfan, with Khalid ibn al-Walid over the idolaters; we prayed Zuhr, and the idolaters said: We had a chance, we had an inattention; had we charged them while they were in prayer. Then the verse of shortening came down between Zuhr and Asr. When Asr came, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood facing the qibla with the idolaters before him; a rank lined behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and after that rank another rank. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bowed and they all bowed; then he prostrated and the rank next to him prostrated, while the others stood guarding them. When these finished the two prostrations and stood, the others who were behind them prostrated; then the rank next to him stepped back to the station of the others, and the last advanced to the station of the first. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bowed and they all bowed; then he prostrated and the rank next to him prostrated, while the others stood guarding them. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the rank next to him sat, the others prostrated, then they all sat, and he greeted them all. He said: He prayed it at Usfan, and he prayed it on the day of Banu Sulaym."
"687","His saying, exalted: 'And whoever does evil or wrongs himself then seeks Allah's forgiveness will find Allah Forgiving, Merciful.' 687 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Jarir narrated, from Layth, from Abu Hubayra, from Ibrahim, he said: Abdillah said: In the Quran there are two verses: no servant commits a sin then recites them and seeks Allah's forgiveness but He forgives him. They asked him about them and he did not tell them. Alqama and al-Aswad, one said to the other: Come with us. They went to the house, took the mushaf, leafed through al-Baqara and said: We did not see them; then they took to al-Nisa until they reached this verse: 'And whoever does evil or wrongs himself...' They said: This is one. Then they leafed through Al Imran until they reached His saying: 'And those who, when they do indecency or wrong themselves, remember Allah and seek forgiveness for their sins - and who forgives sins but Allah - and do not persist in what they did while knowing.' They said: This is another. Then they closed the mushaf and came to Abdillah and said: Are they these two verses? Abdillah said: Yes."
"688","His saying, exalted: 'They call upon besides Him but females, and they call upon but a rebellious Satan.' 688 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Nuh ibn Qays al-Huddani narrated, from Muhammad ibn Sayf, from al-Hasan, he said: There was no clan of the Arabs but it had an idol it worshipped, calling it the female of Banu so-and-so; so Allah revealed: 'They call upon besides Him but females...'"
"689","His saying, exalted: 'then they shall change Allah's creation.' 689 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym and Khalid narrated, from Mughira, from Ibrahim, concerning His statement: 'then they shall change Allah's creation' - he said: Allah's religion."
"690","690 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from Humayd al-A'raj, from Ikrima, he said: It is castration."
"691","691 - Humayd said: So I asked Sa'id ibn Jubayr, and he said: It is the religion of Allah, blessed and exalted."
"692","His saying, exalted: 'It is not by your wishes nor the wishes of the People of the Book; whoever does evil shall be recompensed for it and find for himself besides Allah no protector nor helper. And whoever does of righteous deeds, male or female, while believing, those shall enter Paradise and not be wronged a naqir.' 692 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, he said: The Arabs said: We shall not be raised nor reckoned; and the Christians said: The Fire shall touch us only numbered days; so Allah revealed: 'It is not by your wishes nor the wishes of the People of the Book; whoever does evil shall be recompensed for it.'"
"693","693 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu Mu'awiya narrated, from al-A'mash, from Masruq, concerning His statement: 'It is not by your wishes nor the wishes of the People of the Book' - he said: The Muslims and the People of the Book argued; the Muslims said: We are better guided than you; so Allah revealed: 'It is not by your wishes nor the wishes of the People of the Book'; then the Muslims prevailed over them with this verse: 'And whoever does of righteous deeds, male or female, while believing' to the end of the verse."
"694","694 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhaysin, he heard Muhammad ibn Qays ibn Makhrama telling from Abu Hurayra, he said: When 'whoever does evil shall be recompensed for it' was revealed, that weighed upon the Muslims; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: Draw near and be straight, for everything that befalls the Muslim is expiation, even the thorn he is pricked with and the stumble he stumbles."
"695","695 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Abu Bakr ibn Umara ibn Ruwayba al-Thaqafi, he said: When 'whoever does evil shall be recompensed for it' was revealed, Abu Bakr said: How is soundness after this? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy on you, O Abu Bakr, do you not fall ill? Does hardship not befall you? He said: Then that is for that."
"696","696 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Khalaf ibn Khalifa narrated, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated, he said: Abu Bakr narrated in the time of al-Hajjaj, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him: 'It is not by your wishes nor the wishes of the People of the Book; whoever does evil shall be recompensed for it.' I said: O Messenger of Allah, how is soundness after this? He said: O Abu Bakr, do you not grieve? Do you not sorrow? Does hardship not befall you? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Then this is for this."
"697","697 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu Mu'awiya al-Darir narrated, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Zuhayr, he said: Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, said: How is soundness after this verse: 'whoever does evil shall be recompensed for it'? He said: O Abu Bakr, do you not fall ill? Does hardship not befall you? He said: Yes. He said: That is among what you are recompensed with."
"698","698 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu Mu'awiya narrated, from Asim al-Ahwal, from al-Hasan, concerning His statement: 'whoever does evil shall be recompensed for it' - al-Hasan said: That is only for one Allah, mighty and majestic, intends to disgrace; as for one Allah intends to honor, He overlooks his evil deeds; 'the promise of truth they were promised.'"
"699","699 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abdillah ibn Wahb narrated, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith told me that Bakr ibn Sawada narrated to him that Yazid ibn Abi Yazid narrated to him, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that a man recited this verse: 'whoever does evil shall be recompensed for it,' and said: Shall we be recompensed for every deed we did? We are ruined. That reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Yes, the believer is recompensed with it in this world, in himself, in his body, in what harms him."
"700","700 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu Mu'awiya narrated, from al-A'mash, from Muslim ibn Subayh, he said: Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, how severe is this verse: 'whoever does evil shall be recompensed for it.' The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abu Bakr, the calamity in this world is recompense."
"701","His saying, exalted: 'And if a woman fears from her husband recalcitrance or aversion, there is no blame upon them to make peace between them, and peace is better.' 701 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, that Rafi' ibn Khadij married the daughter of Muhammad ibn Maslama and wanted to divorce her; she said: Do not divorce me, keep me, and apportion for me as you wish to apportion; so Allah revealed: 'And if a woman fears from her husband recalcitrance or aversion, there is no blame upon them to make peace between them'; so the Sunna ran that when a man has a wife who grows old and he dislikes her and wants to divorce her, and she makes peace with him upon a settlement, he may keep her and apportion for her as he wills."
"702","702 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, he said: It was revealed concerning Sawda and her likes: 'And if a woman fears from her husband recalcitrance or aversion.' He said: That is that Sawda bint Zam'a had grown old and feared the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would part from her; she cherished her place with him, and knew of the Messenger of Allah's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) love for Aisha and her station with him; so she gave her day from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) accepted that."
"703","His saying, exalted: 'And you will never be able to do justice between wives, even if you strive; so do not incline wholly and leave her hanging.' 703 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Ibn Sirin, he said: I asked Abida about His statement: 'And you will never be able to do justice between wives, even if you strive.' He said: He gestured with his hand to his chest and said: In love and intercourse."
"704","His saying, exalted: 'And it has been sent down upon you in the Book that when you hear Allah's verses disbelieved in and mocked, do not sit with them until they engage in other talk; indeed you then are like them.' 704 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl ibn Ghazwan narrated, from Ubayd al-Mukattib, from Ibrahim, he said: A man may sit in a gathering and speak a word with which Allah, mighty and majestic, is pleased, and mercy befalls him and encompasses those around him; and a man may sit in a gathering and speak a word with which Allah is angry, and anger befalls him and encompasses those around him."
"705","705 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated, from Hajjaj ibn Dinar, from Amir ibn Shaqiq, from Abu Wa'il, similar to this, and he added in it: 'And it has been sent down upon you in the Book that when you hear Allah's verses disbelieved in and mocked, do not sit with them until they engage in other talk; indeed you then are like them.'"
"706","706 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqama ibn Waqqas al-Laythi, from his father, from his grandfather, from Bilal ibn al-Harith, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: A man speaks a word of Allah's pleasure, mighty and majestic, not thinking it reaches what it reached, and Allah writes for him by it His pleasure until the day he meets Him; and a man speaks a word of Allah's anger, not thinking it reaches what it reached, and Allah writes for him by it His anger until the day he meets Him."
"707","His saying, exalted: 'Allah does not love the public utterance of evil in speech except by one wronged.' 707 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Bakr, from Mujahid, concerning His statement: 'Allah does not love the public utterance of evil in speech except by one wronged' - he said: It is a man you seek hospitality from and he does not host you; so you are permitted to say it."
"708","His saying, exalted: 'so the thunderbolt seized them for their wrong.' 708 - Sa'id narrated, he said: al-Hakam ibn Zuhayr narrated, from al-Suddi, from Amr ibn Maymun, he said: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, reciting: 'so the stunning seized them.'"
"709","His saying, exalted: 'And there is none of the People of the Book but shall believe in him before his death, and on the Day of Resurrection he shall be a witness against them.' 709 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Attab ibn Bashir narrated, from Khusayf, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, concerning His statement: 'but shall believe in him before his death' - he said: In the recitation of Ubayy it is: 'before their death.' He said: No Jew ever dies until he believes in Isa, peace be upon him. It was said to Ibn Abbas: What if he falls from atop a house? He said: He speaks it in the fall. It was said to him: What if one's neck is struck? He said: He stammers it."
"710","His saying, exalted: 'So for wrong of those who judaized We forbade them good things lawful to them.' 710 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: Ibn Abbas recited: 'good things that had been lawful to them.'"
"711","Chapter of the exegesis of Surat al-Ma'ida; exegesis of Surat al-Ma'ida. 711 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hudayj ibn Mu'awiya narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Maysara, he said: The last sura revealed in the Quran is Surat al-Ma'ida, and in it are seventeen obligations. His saying, exalted: 'O you who believe, do not violate Allah's rites, nor the sacred month, nor the offering, nor the garlands.'"
"712","712 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Khalid ibn Abdillah narrated, from Bayan, he said: I heard al-Sha'bi saying: Nothing of al-Ma'ida was abrogated except this verse: 'O you who believe, do not violate Allah's rites, nor the sacred month, nor the offering, nor the garlands.'"
"713","His saying, exalted: 'Today I perfected for you your religion, completed upon you My favor, and approved for you Islam as religion.' 713 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated, he said: Dawud narrated, from al-Sha'bi, concerning His statement: 'Today I perfected for you your religion' - he said: It was revealed while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood at Arafa, when polytheism had vanished, the landmarks of ignorance were demolished, and no naked one circumambulated the House."
"714","His saying, exalted: 'Today the good things are lawful for you, and the food of those given the Book is lawful for you, and your food is lawful for them.' 714 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, from Ubaydullah ibn Ubayd al-Kala'i, he said: I asked Makhul about the slaughtered animals of the festivals of the People of the Book and those set aside for their churches, and he recited this verse: 'Today the good things are lawful for you, and the food of those given the Book is lawful for you, and your food is lawful for them.' He said: Their food is their slaughtered animals."
"715","His saying, exalted: 'and wipe your heads and your feet to the ankles.' 715 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Khalid narrated, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, that he used to recite: 'so wipe your heads and your feet.' He said: It returns to washing."
"716","716 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Abu Muhammad, freedman of Quraysh, narrated, he said: Abbad ibn al-Rabi' narrated, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that he used to recite it likewise."
"717","717 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Mansur and Abbad narrated, that they heard al-Hasan reciting: 'and your feet.'"
"718","718 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Humayd al-Tawil narrated, from Anas, that he recited: 'and your feet.'"
"719","719 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu Mu'awiya narrated, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, that he used to recite: 'and your feet.'"
"720","720 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated, he said: Dawud and Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated, from al-Sha'bi, that he used to recite: 'and your feet.'"
"721","His saying, exalted: 'so We stirred among them enmity and hatred until the Day of Resurrection.' 721 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated, he said: al-Awwam narrated, from Ibrahim al-Nakha'i, concerning His blessed and exalted saying: 'so We stirred among them enmity and hatred' - he said: I see the stirring in this verse as only the divergent whims and hatred."
"722","722 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated, he said: al-Awwam narrated, he said: I heard Ibrahim al-Nakha'i saying: He set some of them against others in disputation in religion."
"723","723 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated, he said: al-Awwam narrated, from Abu Iyas, he said: Disputes in religion nullify deeds."
"724","His saying, exalted: 'There has come to you from Allah a light and a clear Book; by it Allah guides whoever follows His pleasure the paths of peace.' 724 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from Amr, he heard Ubayd ibn Umayr reciting: 'Allah guides by it.' Sa'id said: A dialect."
"725","His saying, exalted: 'And when Musa said to his people: O my people, remember Allah's favor upon you when He made among you prophets and made you kings and gave you what He gave no one of the worlds.' 725 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu Awana narrated, from Mansur, from al-Hakam, concerning His statement: 'and made you kings' - he said: When one of Banu Isra'il had a house and a servant, he was a king."
"726","726 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, saying: Abu Hani' al-Khawlani informed me that he heard Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli saying: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, when a man asked him: Are we not among the poor Emigrants? Abdullah said to him: Do you have a wife to resort to? He said: Yes. He said: Do you have a dwelling to live in? He said: Yes. He said: Then you are among the rich. He said: I have a servant. He said: Then you are among the kings."
"727","His Exalted saying: {My Lord, I control none but myself and my brother, so separate between us and the transgressing people.} 727 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar: he heard Ubayd ibn Umayr reciting (fa-fruq) with a kasra on the ra."
"728","His Exalted saying: {Because of that We decreed upon the Children of Israel that whoever kills a soul without a soul or corruption in the land, it is as if he killed all mankind, and whoever gives it life, it is as if he gave life to all mankind.} 728 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Ala' ibn Abd al-Karim, from Mujahid, concerning His Exalted saying {whoever kills a soul without a soul or corruption in the land, it is as if he killed all mankind}: he said: in sin. Concerning {and whoever gives it life}: he said: whoever does not kill."
"729","His Exalted saying: {The recompense of those who wage war against Allah and His Messenger and strive in the land causing corruption is that they be killed, or crucified, or their hands and feet be cut off from opposite sides, or they be banished from the land.} 729 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Dawud ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim ibn Abi al-Mukhariq, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, concerning His Exalted saying {The recompense of those who wage war against Allah and His Messenger...}: he said: If the warrior kills, he is killed; if he kills and takes property, he is crucified; if he takes property without killing, his hand and foot are cut off from opposite sides; and if he lurks on the road and frightens travelers without taking property or killing, he is banished from the land."
"730","730 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Abu Hurra narrated to us, from al-Hasan. [Flag: report truncated in source; chain only, no matn stated]"
"731","731 - And Ubaydah, from Ibrahim. [Flag: report truncated in source; chain fragment only, no matn stated]"
"732","732 - And Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak. [Flag: report truncated in source; chain fragment only, no matn stated]"
"733","733 - And Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Ata' and Mujahid. [Flag: report truncated in source; chain fragment only, no matn stated]"
"734","734 - And Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Ata' and Mujahid; they said: The imam has a choice concerning the warrior; whichever of these he wishes, he does."
"735","735 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata', saying: Whatever is in the Qur'an of the form 'or this, or this,' then he has the choice."
"736","736 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, saying: Abd al-Hamid, when he was governor over Iraq, was brought three men who had cut off the road and seized swords, and some people advised him to kill them, so he consulted me and I said to him: Do not do it; I forbade him to kill them because of what I knew of the view of Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz on that, that he did not deem lawful killing anyone in that situation; they kept pressing him until one of them was killed, then some of what I had said weighed on his heart, and some of them wrote to Umar, and his reply came back as a harsh reply condemning what he had done, and in the letter: Why, when you applied this verse and deemed them its people, did you not take the lightest of its penalties? Abu al-Zinad said: Whoever follows their view in Medina claims that the warrior is not the one who steals secretly, hides from the ruler, and raids; rather they said: the warrior is the one who corrupts the progeny of the believers and does not answer the call of the ruler."
"737","His Exalted saying: {As for the male thief and the female thief, cut off their hands as a recompense for what they earned, as an exemplary punishment from Allah, and Allah is Mighty, Wise.} 737 - Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd and Hushaym informed us, from Ibn Awn, from Ibrahim, saying: In our recitation it is: (And the male thieves and the female thieves - their right hands are to be cut)."
"738","His Exalted saying: {And among those who Judaized are listeners to lies, listeners to another people who have not come to you, distorting words from after their places.} 738 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, from Mughira, from Ibrahim: that he used to recite (they distort speech from its places). He said: There used to come down upon them: O sons of my scribes, O sons of my messengers, and they would say: O sons of our firstborns."
"739","His Exalted saying: {Listeners to lies, devourers of ill-gotten gains.} 739 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Khalaf ibn Khalifa narrated to us, saying: Mansur ibn Zadham narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Abu Wa'il, from Masruq, saying: If the judge accepts a gift, he has eaten ill-gotten gain (suht), and if he accepts a bribe, it carries him to disbelief."
"740","740 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Yahya al-Abahh narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, saying: Bribery in judgment is disbelief, and among people it is ill-gotten gain (suht)."
"741","741 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ammar al-Duhni, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Masruq, saying: I asked Ibn Mas'ud about ill-gotten gain (suht): is it bribery in judgment? He said: No; {and whoever does not judge by what Allah sent down, those are the disbelievers,} and the wrongdoers, and the transgressors; rather suht is that a man seeks your help against an injustice and then gives you a gift, and you accept it - that is suht."
"742","742 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay', from Musa ibn Tarif, from his father: that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, distributed something and called a man who calculates, and it was said to him: Why not give him something? He said: If he wishes - but it is suht."
"743","743 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Atiq, saying: Muhammad ibn Sirin used to dislike the fees of the dividers (qussam), saying: They used to say: A bribe for judgment is suht; I do not see any judgment for which a bribe is taken."
"744","744 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Ibn Sirin, saying: He used to dislike stipulation, and saw no harm in a man dividing for a man and being given something without stipulation."
"745","745 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Habib ibn Salih, from Ibn Abbas, saying: Bribery in judgment is suht; so are the fee of the prostitute, the price of the dog, the price of the monkey, the price of the pig, the price of wine, the price of carrion, the price of blood, the stud fee of the stallion, the fee of the wailing woman and the singing woman, the fee of the soothsayer, the fee of the sorcerer, the fee of the tracker (qa'if), the price of predator skins, the price of carrion hides - but if they are tanned there is no harm in them - the fee for making statues, the gift for intercession, and the fee for rescue from drowning."
"746","His Exalted saying: {So if they come to you, judge between them or turn away from them; if you turn away from them, they will not harm you at all.} 746 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Mughira, from al-Sha'bi and Ibrahim; they said: If the People of the Book come before the judges of the Muslims, if he wishes he judges between them, and if he wishes he turns away from them; but if he judges, he judges by what Allah Almighty sent down."
"747","His Exalted saying: {And if you judge, judge between them with justice; indeed Allah loves the just.} 747 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: al-Awwam narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, concerning His Exalted saying {then judge between them with justice}: he said: By stoning."
"748","His Exalted saying: {But how do they make you judge when they have the Torah, in which is the judgment of Allah, then they turn away after that? Those are not believers.} 748 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani narrated to us, saying: I said to Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stone? He said: Yes, he stoned a Jewish man and a Jewish woman. He said: I said: Was that before Surat al-Nur or after it? He said: I do not know."
"749","His Exalted saying: {Indeed We sent down the Torah, in which is guidance and light; the prophets who submitted judged by it for those who Judaized, and the rabbis and scholars, by what they were entrusted of the Book of Allah, and they were witnesses over it; so do not fear people but fear Me, and do not sell My verses for a small price; and whoever does not judge by what Allah sent down, those are the disbelievers,} up to His Exalted saying {and whoever does not judge by what Allah sent down, those are the wrongdoers.} 749 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hujayr, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, concerning His Exalted saying {and whoever does not judge by what Allah sent down, those are the disbelievers}: he said: It is not the disbelief that you think of."
"750","750 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, saying: Allah Almighty only sent down {and whoever does not judge by what Allah sent down, those are the disbelievers,} and {the wrongdoers,} and {the transgressors,} specifically concerning the Jews."
"751","751 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'ida narrated to us, saying: al-Sha'bi narrated to us, saying: This verse {and whoever does not judge by what Allah sent down, those are the disbelievers} was revealed about the people of Islam; {and whoever does not judge by what Allah sent down, those are the wrongdoers} - he said: it was revealed about the Jews; {then those are the transgressors} - he said: it was revealed about the Christians."
"752","752 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: al-Awwam narrated to us, from Yusayr: that Umar said: I have never seen the like of one who judges between two people after these three verses: {and whoever does not judge by what Allah sent down, those are the disbelievers,} and {the wrongdoers} - I have never seen the like of one who judges between two people."
"753","753 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: al-Mughira narrated to us, from Ibrahim, concerning the people of the dhimma when they are made to swear: they are made strict upon them by their religion, and when the oath is due they are made to swear by Allah."
"754","754 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Mughira narrated to us, saying: Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz wrote that no one is to be made to swear by anything other than Allah."
"755","755 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Malik narrated to us, saying: They are made to swear by Allah, and the Torah and the Gospel are indeed among the books of Allah Almighty."
"756","756 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Masruq: that he used to make the People of the Book swear by Allah Almighty."
"757","757 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Husayn narrated to us, from one who narrated to him, from Ibn Abbas, concerning His Exalted saying: {then whoever gives it as charity, it is an expiation for him}: he said: an expiation for the injurer."
"758","758 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Husayn, from Ibn Abbas, the same."
"759","759 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Mughira narrated to us, from Mujahid, saying: For the injurer; and Ibrahim said: For the injured."
"760","760 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, concerning His Exalted saying: {then whoever gives it as charity, it is an expiation for him}: he said: The one who was afflicted; and the injured one's reward is upon Allah."
"761","761 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq: he heard Abu Ishaq asking Mujahid about His Exalted saying: {then whoever gives it as charity, it is an expiation for him}: he said: For the injurer."
"762","762 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Imran ibn Zibyan, from Adi ibn Thabit: that a man knocked out the mouth of a man in the time of Mu'awiya, and blood-money was offered to him but he refused except retaliation; he was offered two blood-moneys and refused; he was offered three, then a man among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Whoever gives charity of blood down to less than it, it is an expiation for him from the day he was born until the day he dies."
"763","His Exalted saying: {And We sent down to you the Book in truth, confirming what is before it of the Book and dominant over it.} 763 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hudayj ibn Mu'awiya narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from a man of Banu Tamim, from Ibn Abbas, concerning His saying: {and dominant over it}: he said: Entrusted over it."
"764","His Exalted saying: {Do they then seek the judgment of ignorance? And who is better than Allah in judgment for a people who are certain?} 764 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Tawus: that he was asked about a man who favors some of his children over others, and he recited: {Do they then seek the judgment of ignorance?}"
"765","His Exalted saying: {Perhaps Allah will bring victory or a command from Him, and they will become regretful over what they concealed in themselves.} 765 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr: he heard Ibn al-Zubayr reciting: (Perhaps Allah will bring victory or a command from Him, and the transgressors will become regretful over what they concealed in themselves). Amr said: I do not know whether it was a recitation or an explanation."
"766","His Exalted saying: {O you who believe, whoever of you turns back from his religion - Allah will bring a people He loves.} 766 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us, from al-Sari ibn Yahya, from al-Hasan, concerning His Exalted saying: {Allah will bring a people He loves and who love Him}: he said: The guardianship of Allah - by Allah - Abu Bakr and his companions."
"767","His Exalted saying: {Why do the rabbis and scholars not forbid them from their sinful speech and their devouring of ill-gotten gains? Evil is what they used to do.} 767 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, concerning His Exalted saying: {Why do the rabbis and scholars not forbid them from their sinful speech}: he said: The rabbaniyyun are the jurists, the scholars, and they are above the ahbar."
"768","His Exalted saying: {O Messenger, convey what was sent down to you from your Lord; if you do not, you have not conveyed His message; and Allah will protect you from people; indeed Allah does not guide the disbelieving people.} 768 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: al-Harith ibn Ubayd al-Iyadi narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Iyas al-Jurayri, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to be guarded, then there came down: {O Messenger, convey what was sent down to you from your Lord... and Allah will protect you from people}. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put his head out of the dome and said: O people, disperse, for Allah has protected me from people."
"769","His Exalted saying: {Indeed those who believed, and those who Judaized, and the Sabians, and the Christians - whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day and does righteousness, there is no fear upon them nor shall they grieve.} 769 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to us, from his father, saying: I asked Aisha about the lapse of the Qur'an: {Indeed those who believed, and those who Judaized, and the Sabians,} and {and those who establish prayer and give zakah,} and {indeed these two are sorcerers}: she said: O son of my sister, this is the work of the scribes; they erred in the writing."
"770","His Exalted saying: {Cursed were those who disbelieved among the Children of Israel upon the tongue of David and Jesus son of Mary; that was for what they disobeyed and used to transgress.} 770 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Husayn, from Abu Malik, concerning His Exalted saying: {Cursed were those who disbelieved among the Children of Israel upon the tongue of David and Jesus son of Mary}: he said: Whoever was cursed upon the tongue of David became pigs, and whoever was cursed upon the tongue of Jesus son of Mary became monkeys. It was said: Was the recitation before that? He said: Yes."
"771","His Exalted saying: {O you who believe, do not forbid the good things Allah made lawful for you, and do not transgress; indeed Allah does not love the transgressors.} 771 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Husayn, from Abu Malik, concerning His Exalted saying: {O you who believe, do not forbid the good things Allah made lawful for you}: he said: It was revealed about Uthman ibn Maz'un and his companions; they forbade upon themselves many good things and women, and one of them intended to cut off his organ, so Allah Almighty sent down: {O you who believe, do not forbid the good things Allah made lawful for you, and do not transgress; indeed Allah does not love the transgressors.}"
"772","772 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, saying: Abdullah was brought an udder and began eating from it, and said to the people: Come near. The people drew near but one man kept away, so Abdullah said to him: What is the matter with you? He said: I forbade the udder upon myself. He said: This is among the footsteps of Satan; come near and eat, and expiate your oath. Then he recited: {O you who believe, do not forbid the good things Allah made lawful for you,} up to His saying {the transgressors.}"
"773","773 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Hammam, from Amr ibn Shurahbil: that Ma'qil ibn Muqarrin came to Abdullah and said: He forbade the bed upon himself. Abdullah said to him: {O you who believe, do not forbid the good things Allah made lawful for you,} up to His saying {the transgressors.} Free a slave. He said: I only recited the verse last night, then came to you. He said: My slave stole a qaba' from me. He said: Your wealth stole part of itself in part. He said: I think he mentioned: My slave-girl fornicated. He said: Flog her. He said: She was never married. He said: Her being married is her Islam."
"774","774 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Hammam: that Ma'qil asked Ibn Mas'ud, saying: I swore not to sleep on my bed for a year. Abdullah recited: {O you who believe, do not forbid the good things Allah made lawful for you...} the verse, then said: Expiate your oath. He said: Which oaths are purest? He said: Freeing a slave. He said: My slave stole my qaba's - shall I cut him? Abdullah said: No; your wealth is part of itself in part. He said: My slave-girl fornicated - shall I flog her? He said: Flog her. Abdullah said: Flog her fifty. He said: If she returns? He said: Flog her fifty."
"775","His Exalted saying: {Allah does not hold you for idle talk in your oaths, but He holds you for what you have contracted of oaths.} 775 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Mughira narrated to us, from Ibrahim, concerning His Exalted saying: {Allah does not hold you for idle talk in your oaths}: he said: It is a man who swears about a matter thinking it is as he swore, but it is not so. He said: He expiates his oath."
"776","776 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Abu Bishr narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, saying: Idle talk is that a man swears to commit a sin, and Allah does not hold him if he abandons it, but holds him if he acts upon it. I said to Abu Bishr: What should he do? He said: He expiates his oath and abandons the sin."
"777","777 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Khalid narrated to us, from Mughira, from Ibrahim, saying: It is a man who swears about something then thinks it is so, though it is not so."
"778","778 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Khalid narrated to us, from Husayn, from Abu Malik, the same."
"779","779 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Khalid narrated to us, from Mughira, from Amir al-Sha'bi, saying: It is people's saying: No, by Allah, and Yes, by Allah, without intending an oath."
"780","780 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Khalid narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik, from Ata', from Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her: that Ubayd ibn Umayr asked her about idle oaths, and she said the same as al-Sha'bi said."
"781","781 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Aisha, saying: It is a man's saying: No, by Allah, and Yes, by Allah."
"782","782 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Khalid narrated to us, from Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Wasim, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, saying: Idle oaths are that you swear while angry."
"783","783 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Attab ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, saying: It is: No, by Allah, and Yes, by Allah."
"784","784 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Husayn narrated to us, from Abu Malik, saying: Oaths are three: an oath that is expiated, an oath that is not expiated, and an oath for which its swearer is not held. As for the oath that is expiated, it is a man who pledges not to do such-and-such, then does it - upon him is expiation. As for the oath that is not expiated, it is a man who swears about a matter deliberately lying - there is no expiation in it. And as for the oath for which its swearer is not held, it is a man who swears about a matter thinking it is as he swore, but it is not so - this is what has no expiation in it, and it is idle talk."
"785","His Exalted saying: {Its expiation is feeding ten needy of the average of what you feed your families, or clothing them, or freeing a slave; whoever does not find, then fasting three days; that is the expiation of your oaths when you swear; and guard your oaths.} 785 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from Yasar ibn Numayr, saying: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: A man comes to me asking me, and I swear not to give him, then it occurs to me and I give him; so when I command you to expiate for me, feed ten needy, for each needy half a sa' of wheat, or a sa' of barley or dates."
"786","786 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from Yasar ibn Numayr, saying: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said to me: When I command you to expiate for me, give each needy half a sa' of wheat."
"787","787 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us, saying: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Yasar ibn Numayr, saying: Umar ibn al-Khattab said to me: I swear not to give some people, then it occurs to me to give them; so when you see me do that, feed ten needy on my behalf - between every two needy a sa' of wheat, or a sa' of dates."
"788","788 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Yarfa, saying: Umar ibn al-Khattab said to me: I placed myself regarding the wealth of Allah Almighty in the position of the guardian of the orphan: if I need, I take from it, and when I am at ease I return it, and if I am independent I abstain; and I have been put in charge of a great matter of the Muslims; so when you hear me swear an oath and not fulfill it, feed ten needy on my behalf - five sa's of wheat, between every two needy a sa'."
"789","789 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, saying: I found the people giving a mudd each in the food of the needy, and deeming that sufficient for them."
"790","790 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, saying: Abu Ja'far, the freedman of Ibn Ayyash, informed me, from Abdullah ibn Abbas: that he said concerning the expiation of oaths: A white mudd for each needy."
"791","791 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Ya'qub ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Ja'far, the freedman of Ibn Ayyash, from Abdullah ibn Abbas, the same."
"792","792 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim ibn Abi Umayya, from Mujahid, saying: Every feeding in the Qur'an is half a sa'."
"793","793 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Attab ibn Bashir narrated to us, saying: Khusayf narrated to us, from Ata' and Mujahid and Ikrima, concerning the expiation of oaths, saying: For each needy two mudds: a mudd for his condiment, and a mudd he eats at his lunch and dinner."
"794","794 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, concerning the expiation of oaths, saying: A makkuuk of dates, and a makkuuk of wheat; and if he invites them and feeds them bread and meat, or bread and oil, or bread and ghee, or bread and milk, that suffices for him."
"795","795 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'ida narrated to us, from Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Husayn al-Harithi, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: that he said concerning the expiation of oaths: He gives them lunch and dinner - bread and meat, bread and oil, bread and ghee."
"796","796 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated to us, saying: I was told, from Ibrahim, that he used to say: He gives them lunch and dinner; and al-Hasan used to say: A single meal suffices."
"797","797 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Yunus narrated to us, from al-Hasan: that he used to say: Concerning the food of the needy, a single meal; but if he gives them into their hands, then a makkuuk of wheat and a makkuuk of dates."
"798","798 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Abi al-Mughira, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, concerning His Exalted saying: {of the average of what you feed your families}: he said: The elder used to have better than the younger, and the free better than the slave, so they were commanded to a middle of that - neither its highest nor its lowest."
"799","799 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Salama ibn Alqama narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin: that Abu Musa al-Ash'ari swore an oath and expiated; he ordered the needy and they were brought into the treasury, and he ordered a bowl of tharid which was set before them, and they ate; then he clothed each of them with a garment - either a mu'aqqad or a zahrani."
"800","800 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, saying: I heard him when asked about the saying of Allah Almighty: {or clothing them} - in the expiation of oaths - he said: For each needy an aba'a and a turban."
"801","801 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Khalid narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, the same."
"802","802 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Mughira narrated to us, from Ibrahim, saying: A garment each; for each needy a comprehensive garment."
"803","803 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Attab ibn Bashir narrated to us, saying: Khusayf narrated to us, from Ata' and Mujahid and Ikrima, saying: For each needy a garment: a shirt, or a waist-wrapper, or a cloak. I said to Khusayf: What if he is wealthy? He said: Whichever of these he does is good; and whoever does not find any of these qualities, then fasting three days; and he mentioned that in the recitation of Ubayy it is: (consecutive)."
"804","804 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Ibrahim, saying: In our recitation concerning the expiation of oaths: (three consecutive days)."
"805","805 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Hajjaj informed me, saying: I asked Ata' about fasting in the expiation of oaths. He said: If he wishes, he separates them. I said: But in the recitation of Abdullah it is (consecutive). He said: Then we submit to the Book of Allah Almighty."
"806","806 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Tawus, saying: If he wishes, he separates them. Mujahid said to him: In the recitation of Abdullah it is (consecutive). He said: Then it is consecutive."
"807","807 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Abi Humayd, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla: that a man from the people of the West came to Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: By Allah, O Commander of the Faithful, you shall provide me a mount. Umar looked at the nearest of them to him and said: By Allah, if you are such that you inform me of your need without swearing at me, while I swear by Allah that I will not provide you a mount - I think he repeated it thirty times, or nearly thirty times. Then a man called Atik ibn Bilal al-Ansari said: What do you want? Do you not see that the Commander of the Faithful has sworn oaths I cannot count that he will not provide you a mount? By Allah, you intend nothing but evil. The man said: By Allah, it is indeed the wealth of Allah; by Allah, I am indeed among the dependents of Allah; by Allah, you are indeed the Commander of the Faithful; my mount has perished under me; by Allah, I am a wayfarer cut off; by Allah, you shall provide me a mount. Umar said to him: How did you say? He repeated it to him, and Umar said: By Allah, the wealth is indeed the wealth of Allah; you are indeed among the dependents of Allah; I am indeed the Commander of the Faithful; if your mount has perished under you, I will not leave you to destruction; by Allah, I shall provide you a mount. He repeated it until he swore thirty oaths, or two oaths, then said: I never swear an oath and then see something better than it except that I follow the better of the two oaths."
"808","His Exalted saying: {O you who believe, wine and gambling and idols and divining arrows are filth from the work of Satan, so avoid them that you may prosper. Satan only wants to cause enmity and hatred among you through wine and gambling, and to turn you from remembrance of Allah and from prayer; so will you desist?} up to His saying {and Allah loves the doers of good.} 808 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hazm ibn Abi Hazm al-Quta'i narrated to us, saying: I heard al-Hasan saying: Some of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to drink wine, and most of their livelihood was from it; when its prohibition came down, some people said: Wine has been forbidden to us, though so-and-so and so-and-so used to drink it and they are among the people of Paradise, and they died - they used to drink it; its prohibition was only sent down, and this verse came down: {O you who believe, wine and gambling and idols and divining arrows are filth from the work of Satan, so avoid them,} up to His saying: {so will you desist?} The people said: We have desisted, our Lord. Then He said: {There is no sin upon those who believed and did righteousness for what they tasted} - the people who used to drink it then died before its prohibition came down - {when they feared and believed and did righteousness, then feared and believed, then feared and did good; and Allah loves the doers of good.}"
"809","809 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr: he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: Some people drank wine in the morning on the day of Uhud, then were killed."
"810","810 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Abi Aruba narrated to us, from Qatada, concerning His Exalted saying: {They ask you about wine and gambling; say: In them is great sin and benefits for people, but their sin is greater than their benefit}: he said: Allah condemned it in this verse but did not forbid it, and it was then lawful; then Allah sent down after that a verse about wine sterner than this verse, saying: {O you who believe, do not approach prayer while intoxicated until you know what you say}. So intoxication was thereby unlawful; then Allah Almighty sent down the verse in Surat al-Ma'ida: {O you who believe, wine and gambling and idols and divining arrows are filth from the work of Satan, so avoid them...} up to His Exalted saying: {so will you desist?} Qatada said: Its prohibition came in this verse - its little and its much, what intoxicates of it and what does not intoxicate."
"811","811 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatada, saying: It reached us that when this verse came down: {Wine and gambling are...} the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O people, Allah Almighty has forbidden wine; so whoever has any of it, let him neither taste it nor sell it. So they poured it out, until the Muslims smelled its odor in the road of Medina."
"812","812 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Abu Hayyan al-Taymi narrated to us, saying: Shaddad Abu al-Furat narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud, a shaykh - or he said, a man of the people of al-Mada'in - narrated to me, saying: I was beneath the pulpit of Hudhayfa while he was addressing the people at al-Mada'in, and he said: O people, what is with peoples who, it reached me, sell wine and keep pigs? Indeed the seller of wine and its drinker are equal in sin, and the keeper of the pig and its eater are equal in sin. O people, look after your slaves and see what earnings they bring you, for no flesh grown from ill-gotten gain (suht) shall enter Paradise."
"813","813 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Abi Aruba narrated to us, from Qatada, saying: Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab said: Wine was only called khamr because it was left until its clear part clarified and its sediment settled."
"814","814 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Mansur narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Khaythama ibn Abd al-Rahman, saying: Abdullah ibn Amr said: Whoever drinks wine remains a polytheist that day until evening; if he becomes intoxicated by it, his prayer is not accepted for forty days; if he dies during them, he dies a disbeliever."
"815","815 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, saying: Wine is cursed, and its drinker, its pourer, its seller, its buyer, its presser, the one for whom it is pressed, its carrier, the one to whom it is carried, and the eater of its price."
"816","816 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Wa'il al-Ansari, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah cursed wine, and cursed its drinker and its pourer, its presser and the one for whom it is pressed, its carrier and the one to whom it is carried, its seller and its buyer, and the eater of its price."
"817","817 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: al-Awwam narrated to us, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi', from Abdullah ibn Amr. [Flag: report truncated in source; chain only, no matn stated]"
"818","818 - And Ubaydah narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Abdullah ibn Amr, saying: The habitual drinker of wine is like one who worshipped al-Lat and al-Uzza."
"819","819 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Muti' ibn Abdullah narrated to us, saying: al-Sha'bi narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, saying: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: May Allah curse so-and-so, for he was the first to permit selling wine; and trade is only lawful in what is lawful to eat or drink."
"820","820 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hibban ibn Ali narrated to us, saying: Abu Sinan Dirar ibn Murra narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, saying: Abdullah ibn Umar said: If I saw anyone drinking wine and he did not see me, I would kill him; if I were able to kill him, I would kill him."
"821","821 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Fulayh, meaning Ibn Sulayman, narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Wa'la, saying: I asked Ibn Abbas: We are in a land where we have vines, and most of its produce is wine? Ibn Abbas said: A man of Daws came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a skin of wine as a gift to him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do you know that Allah forbade it after you? The Dawsi turned to a man with him and ordered him to sell it, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do you know that the One who forbade drinking it forbade selling it and eating its price? Then he ordered the waterskin and it was poured out until not a drop remained in it."
"822","822 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, from a man, from Abu Hurayra: that a man gave the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a skin of wine as a gift, as he used to gift it to him, and he said: Allah forbade it after you. He said: Shall I not sell it? He said: The One who forbade us drinking it forbade us selling it. He said: Shall I not gift it to the Jews? He mentioned that he informed him: The One who forbade drinking it forbade them gifting it to the Jews. He said: What shall I do? He said: Pour it in al-Batha'."
"823","823 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ja'da: I heard him saying: Uthman said on the pulpit: Beware of wine, for it is the key to every evil; a man of those before you was told: either prostrate to this cross, or burn this book, or kill this boy, or assault this woman, or drink this cup - wine - and he deemed it the lightest for him; when he drank it, he did all that: he prostrated to the cross, burned the book, killed the boy, and assaulted the woman."
"824","824 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Ya'qub ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Ata' ibn Abi Rabah: that Abdullah ibn Abbas said: The greatest of major sins is drinking wine."
"825","825 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Shubayl ibn Awf, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, saying: It reached Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, about a man in al-Sawad who traded in wine and grew rich and his wealth increased; so Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, wrote concerning him: Break up every wealth of his you find, and let loose every livestock of his."
"826","826 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, saying: Everything involving gambling is of maysir, even children's play with walnuts and knucklebones."
"827","827 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Jarir narrated to us, from Mughira, from Ibrahim: that he used to dislike children's gambling."
"828","His Exalted saying: {O you who believe, do not kill game while you are in pilgrim sanctity; whoever of you kills it deliberately, the recompense is the like of what he killed of livestock.} 828 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, concerning His Exalted saying: {whoever of you kills it deliberately}: he said: Deliberate in killing it, forgetful of his ihram - that is the one upon whom judgment is passed."
"829","829 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, concerning His Exalted saying: {whoever of you kills it deliberately}: he said: I see nothing in a mistake."
"830","830 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Ata', concerning His Exalted saying: {whoever of you kills it deliberately}: he said: Whoever kills game then repeats, the recompense is repeated upon him."
"831","831 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Ata', saying: Judgment is passed upon him another time."
"832","832 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, concerning His saying: {the recompense is the like of what he killed of livestock}: he said: If the pilgrim in ihram hits game, its recompense is judged upon him; if he has its recompense with him, he slaughters it and gives its meat in charity; if he does not have its recompense, its recompense is valued in dirhams, then the dirhams are valued in food, and he fasts a day in place of every half sa'; food was only intended for the fasting; and when the food is found, its recompense is found."
"833","His Exalted saying: {Lawful to you is the game of the sea and its food, as enjoyment for you and for travelers.} 833 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Mijlaz, from Ibn Abbas, concerning His Exalted saying: {Lawful to you is the game of the sea and its food, as enjoyment for you}: he said: Its food is what it casts forth."
"834","834 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Khalid narrated to us, from Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, concerning His saying: {Lawful to you is the game of the sea and its food}: he said: Its game is the fresh, and its food is the salted, for the traveler and the resident."
"835","835 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Khalaf ibn Khalifa narrated to us, saying: Husayn narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, saying: Its game is what is hunted, and its food is what the sea casts out."
"836","836 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, saying: I came to al-Bahrayn and its people asked me about what the sea casts forth of fish, and I ordered them to eat it; when I came, I asked Umar about that, and he said: What did you order them? I said: I ordered them to eat it. He said: Had you said otherwise, I would have struck you with the stick. Then Umar recited: {Lawful to you is the game of the sea and its food}. He said: Its game is what is hunted, and its food is what it casts forth."
"837","837 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, saying: Game is not lawful to you while you are in ihram; and he recited: {And forbidden to you is the game of the land as long as you are in pilgrim sanctity.}"
"838","838 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim al-Basri, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, saying: It is unrestricted."
"839","His Exalted saying: {O you who believe, do not ask about things which, if disclosed to you, would displease you; if you ask about them while the Qur'an is being sent down, they will be disclosed to you; Allah pardoned them, and Allah is Forgiving, Forbearing. A people before you asked about them, then became disbelievers therein. Allah made no bahira, nor sa'iba, nor wasila, nor ham; but those who disbelieved invent lies against Allah, and most of them do not understand.} 839 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Attab narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, concerning His Exalted saying: {do not ask about things}: he said: Meaning the bahira, the sa'iba, the wasila, and the ham - do you not see that He says: Allah made no such-and-such? As for Ikrima, he said: They used to ask about the verses, and were forbidden that. Then He said: {A people before you asked about them, then became disbelievers therein}. I said: Mujahid narrated to me otherwise, from Ibn Abbas - why do you say this? He said: Hah."
"840","His Exalted saying: {O you who believe, upon you is yourselves; he who strayed will not harm you when you are guided; to Allah is your return all together, and He will inform you of what you used to do.} 840 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays, saying: I heard Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, saying on the pulpit: People recite this verse without knowing its place: {O you who believe, upon you is yourselves; he who strayed will not harm you when you are guided}. When sins are committed among a people and they do not denounce them, and they see the wrongdoer and do not change him, Allah envelops them in punishment."
"841","841 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Ubayd Allah ibn Jarir, from his father, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no man among a people in which sins are committed, able to change them but not changing them, except that Allah afflicts them with punishment before they die."
"842","842 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hazm ibn Abi Hazm narrated to us, saying: I heard al-Hasan saying: A man among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: {O you who believe, upon you is yourselves; he who strayed will not harm you when you are guided}. He said: Then someone said: Leave mentioning this verse; it is not for you; when it is accepted from you, then it is for you."
"843","843 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Yunus narrated to us, from al-Hasan, saying: Ibn Mas'ud was asked about this verse, and he said: It is accepted from you today, so say it; when it is rejected against you, then upon you is yourselves."
"844","844 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Juwaybir narrated to us, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn Mas'ud, concerning His Exalted saying: {O you who believe, upon you is yourselves}: he said: Enjoin good and forbid evil, as long as it is short of the whip and the sword; when it reaches that, then upon you is yourselves."
"845","845 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, concerning His saying: {upon you is yourselves; he who strayed will not harm you}: meaning the People of the Book."
"846","846 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abu Awana and Jarir narrated to us, from Mu'awiya ibn Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, saying: I said to Ibn Abbas: Shall I command my ruler to good? He said: If you fear he will kill you, do not; if you must do it, then between you and him. And Abu Awana added: And do not backbite your ruler."
"847","847 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, saying: A man said to Umar ibn al-Khattab: Not fearing the blame of a blamer for Allah is better for me, or attending to myself? He said: As for whoever is in charge of any affair of the Muslims, he does not fear the blame of a blamer for Allah; and whoever is private, let him attend to his own self and advise his ruler."
"848","848 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mis'ar, saying: A man came to Abdullah and said: Advise me. He said: When you hear Allah saying: O you who believe, lend it your ear, for it is either good you are commanded to, or evil you are turned from."
"849","849 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Ibn Mas'ud, concerning His Exalted saying: {upon you is yourselves}: he said: This is not its time; you say it as long as it is accepted from you; when it is rejected against you, then upon you is yourselves - he who strayed will not harm you when you are guided."
"850","850 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Jarir narrated to us, from al-Ala' ibn al-Musayyab, from Khaythama, saying: Abdullah said: When you come to the appointed commander, do not come to him over people's heads."
"851","His Exalted saying: {O you who believe, testimony between you when death approaches one of you at the time of bequest: two just men among you, or two others from other than you,} up to His saying: {and we did not transgress; indeed then we would be among the wrongdoers.} 851 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym and Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Shurayh: that he would not allow the testimony of a Jew or a Christian against Muslims except in a bequest, and would not allow it in a bequest except while traveling."
"852","852 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, concerning His Exalted saying: {or two others from other than you}: that is, from other than your religious community."
"853","853 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Mughira narrated to us, from Ibrahim. [Flag: report truncated in source; chain only, no matn stated]"
"854","854 - al-Mughira said: And one who heard Sa'id ibn Jubayr saying that informed me. [Flag: matn elided in source; refers to preceding report]"
"855","855 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Ibn Sirin, from Abidah: that he said the same."
"856","856 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Dawud, from al-Sha'bi, from Shurayh, concerning His Exalted saying: {or two others from other than you}: he said: If a man dies in a land of estrangement and finds no Muslim, and takes two non-Muslim witnesses, their testimony is allowed; but if two Muslims come and testify otherwise, the testimony of the Muslims is taken and theirs is left."
"857","857 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'ida narrated to us, saying: al-Sha'bi narrated to us: that a man approached death at Daquqa' and found none of the Muslims to witness his bequest, so he took two men of the People of the Book as witnesses; they came with his estate to Abu Musa al-Ash'ari and informed him. al-Ash'ari said: This is a matter that did not occur after what occurred in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He made them swear after the Asr prayer by Allah that they had not betrayed, nor lied, nor altered, and that it was indeed his estate; then he allowed their testimony."
"858","858 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, concerning His Exalted saying: {two just men among you, or two others from other than you}: he said: From the Muslims; except that he says: from the tribe, or from other than the tribe."
"859","859 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Shu'ba, from Qatada, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, concerning His Exalted saying: {two just men among you, or two others from other than you}: he said: From the People of the Book."
"860","860 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata', from Ibn Abbas, saying: I heard him saying: {from those upon whom the first right devolved,} and saying: What if the first two were minors?"
"861","861 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, from Mughira, from Ibrahim: that he used to recite: {from those upon whom the first right devolved.}"
"862","862 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from al-Sha'bi: that he used to recite: (And we do not conceal testimony; indeed then we would be among the sinners)."
"863","His Exalted saying: {When the disciples said: O Jesus son of Mary, can your Lord send down to us a table from heaven? He said: Fear Allah if you are believers.} 863 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Abu Muhammad, the freedman of Quraysh, narrated to us, from Abbad ibn al-Rabi', from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: that he used to recite: {can you (tastati')}."
"864","864 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Husayn narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, the same."
"865","865 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Husayn, from Ibn Abi Ismail, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: that he used to recite: {Can you (tastati') your Lord}."
"866","866 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Awf narrated to us, from al-Hasan: that he used to recite: {Can He (yastati')}."
"867","867 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Mughira narrated to us, from Ibrahim, saying: Our companions used to recite likewise."
"868","868 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: that he used to recite: {Can you (tastati') your Lord}."
"869","869 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu Abd al-Rahman: that he used to recite: {Can you (tastati')}."
"870","Chapter of the interpretation of Surat al-An'am, verse 19. His Exalted saying: {And this Qur'an was revealed to me that I may warn you by it.} 870 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b, concerning His Exalted saying: {And this Qur'an was revealed to me that I may warn you by it and whomever it reaches}: he said: Whoever the Qur'an reaches has been conveyed to by Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"871","Verse (23), His saying, Exalted is He: {By Allah, our Lord, we were not polytheists}. 871 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Sha'bi reciting it {By Allah, our Lord}. I said to him: Our companions recite it {By Allah, our Lord}! He said: Thus did 'Alqamah teach it to me."
"872","872 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from 'Asim ibn Bahdalah, he said: The companions of 'Abdullah used to recite it {By Allah, our Lord}, and Abu 'Abd al-Rahman used to recite it {By Allah, our Lord}."
"873","873 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Sha'bi, from 'Alqamah, that he used to recite it: {By Allah, our Lord}."
"874","Verse (26), His saying, Exalted is He: {And they forbid from it and keep away from it}. 874 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hammad ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from one who heard Ibn 'Abbas saying: ""And they forbid from it and keep away from it"" was revealed concerning Abu Talib; he used to forbid that he (the Prophet) be harmed, while keeping away from what he brought."
"875","875 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from some of his shaykhs, he said: Abu Talib used to forbid his killing and keep away from following him."
"876","Verse (33), His saying, Exalted is He: {We know well that what they say grieves you; for they do not deny you, but the wrongdoers reject the signs of Allah}. 876 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b, that he used to recite: {for they do not deny you} - he said, he said: They do not nullify what is in your hands."
"877","877 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Abu Muhammad, freedman of Quraysh, narrated to us, from 'Abbad ibn al-Rabi', from 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: He used to recite {for they do not deny you} unaccented (light)."
"878","Verse (44), His saying, Exalted is He: {So when they forgot what they were reminded of, We opened for them the doors of everything, until when they rejoiced in what they were given, We seized them suddenly, and behold, they were in despair}. 878 - Sa'id narrated, he said: I heard Sufyan saying regarding {So when they forgot what they were reminded of, We opened for them the doors of everything}, he said: The comfort of worldly life and its ease, until when they rejoiced in what they were given, We seized them suddenly."
"879","Verse (52), His saying, Exalted is He: {And do not drive away those who call upon their Lord morning and evening, seeking His Face}. 879 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {And do not drive away those who call upon their Lord morning and evening} - he said: Do not drive them away from remembrance."
"880","Verse (57), His saying, Exalted is He: {Judgment belongs to none but Allah; He relates the truth, and He is the best of deciders}. 880 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from 'Ata, from Ibn 'Abbas - that he used to recite {He relates (yaqussu) the truth}, saying: {We relate to you the best of stories}."
"881","Verse (59), His saying, Exalted is He: {And no leaf falls but He knows it}. 881 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Masruq, from Hassan al-Numayri, from Ibn 'Abbas, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {And no leaf falls but He knows it} - he said: There is no tree on land or sea except that an angel is assigned to it, recording what falls of its leaves."
"882","Verse (65), His saying, Exalted is He: {Say: He is Able to send upon you torment from above you, or from beneath your feet, or to confound you into factions and make some of you taste the violence of others}. 882 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd and Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn 'Abdullah, he said: When {Say: He is Able to send upon you torment from above you} was revealed - the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I seek refuge in Your Face. {Or from beneath your feet} - he said: I seek refuge in Your Face. {Or to confound you into factions and make some of you taste the violence of others} - Sufyan said: It is the lighter one, and Sufyan said: These two are easier."
"883","Verse (75), His saying, Exalted is He: {And thus We showed Ibrahim the dominion of the heavens and the earth, that he might be of the certain}. 883 - Sa'id narrated, he said: al-Hakam ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, he said: al-Suddi - who is Isma'il ibn 'Abd al-Rahman - narrated to me, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {And thus We showed Ibrahim the dominion of the heavens and the earth}, he said: He stood upon a rock, and the seven heavens were opened for him until he looked at the Throne and at his dwelling in Paradise; then the seven earths were opened for him until he looked at the rock upon which the earths rest. That is His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {And We gave him his reward in this world}."
"884","884 - Sa'id narrated, he said: al-Hakam ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Abi Sulaym narrated to me, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Salman al-Farisi, he said: When Ibrahim was shown the dominion of the heavens and the earth, he saw a man committing an indecency, so he supplicated against him and he perished; then he saw another committing an indecency, supplicated against him and he perished; then he saw another committing an indecency, supplicated against him and he perished. So Allah revealed to him: O Ibrahim, restrain yourself; you are a man whose supplication is answered, and I deal with My servant in one of three ways: either he repents before death and I accept his repentance, or I bring forth from his loins offspring who remember Me, or he turns away, and Hell is behind him."
"885","Verse (82), His saying, Exalted is He: {Those who believe and do not mix their belief with wrong - those shall have security, and they are guided}. 885 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: al-'Awwam ibn Hawshab narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {Those who believe and do not mix their belief with wrong} - and he did not answer them with anything, until a man came and embraced Islam, and remained only a short while before striving in the way of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and was killed. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This one is of them."
"886","886 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Maysarah, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {Those who believe and do not mix their belief with wrong} - he said: They did not mix it with polytheism."
"887","887 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah, he said: When {Those who believe and do not mix their belief with wrong} was revealed - it weighed heavily upon the people, and they said: O Messenger of Allah, which of us does not wrong himself? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not what you mean; have you not heard what the righteous servant said: {O my son, do not associate with Allah; indeed association is a great wrong}?"
"888","Verse (90), His saying, Exalted is He: {Those are the ones Allah guided, so follow their guidance}. 888 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Shihab ibn Khirash narrated to us, he said: al-'Awwam narrated to me, he said: Mujahid said to me: Regarding what is the prostration in Sad? He said: Allah mentioned the prophets, then said: {Those are the ones Allah guided, so follow their guidance}; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) followed them, and we followed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"889","889 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from al-'Awwam ibn Hawshab, from Mujahid, he said: I said to Ibn 'Abbas: We prostrate in Sad! So he recited: {Those are the ones Allah guided, so follow their guidance} - Dawud was among those whom your Prophet was commanded to follow."
"890","Verse (91), His saying, Exalted is He: {And they did not esteem Allah as He deserves}. 890 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {And they did not esteem Allah as He deserves} - he said: They did not know the true nature of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"891","Verse (95), His saying, Exalted is He: {Indeed Allah splits the grain and the pit}. 891 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Khalid ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, from Husayn, from Abu Malik, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {Splitter of the grain and the pit} - he said: The split that is in the date-pit and the wheat grain."
"892","Verse (98), His saying, Exalted is He: {And He it is who produced you from a single soul; then a dwelling and a repository}. 892 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said: The repository (mustawda') is what is in the loins, and the dwelling (mustaqarr) is what is in the womb, of that which is alive and that which has died."
"893","893 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: Ibn 'Abbas said to me: Marry, O Sa'id! I said: That is not in my mind today! He said: Even if you say that, whatever repository is in your loins shall surely come forth."
"894","894 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, he said: I heard 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud saying: When a man's decreed term is in a land, a need for him is created there; then when he reaches the utmost of his term - his term ends - he is taken, and the earth will say on the Day of Resurrection: O Lord, this is what You entrusted to me."
"895","895 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Ibrahim, he said: 'Abdullah said: Its repository is in this world, and its dwelling is in the womb."
"896","896 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu al-Malih, from a man of his people, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah wills to take a servant in a land, He creates for him a need there."
"897","897 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mansur narrated to us, from al-Hasan, that he used to recite {then a dwelling and a repository}."
"898","898 - Sa'id narrated, he said: 'Ubaydah ibn Humayd al-Hadhdha' narrated to us, he said: 'Ammar al-Duhni narrated to us, from Hammad al-Madini, from Kurayb, he said: Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah have mercy on him, summoned me and said: Write: From 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas to so-and-so, the scholar of Tayma, peace be upon you; I praise to you Allah, besides whom there is no god. I said: You begin by saying peace be upon you? He said: Allah is Peace. Write: Peace be upon you; as for what follows, inform me about the dwelling and the repository, and about a Garden whose width is the heavens and the earth. He said: So I took the letter to the Jew and gave it to him; when he looked at it he said: Welcome to the letter of my friend among the Muslims! He took me to his house and opened many scrolls of his, throwing those scrolls aside without turning to them. I said: What is the matter with you? He said: These are scrolls the Jews wrote - until he brought out the scroll of Musa, looked into it and said: The repository is the loins, and the dwelling is the womb. Then he recited this verse: {And We settle in the wombs what We will} and {And for you on earth is a dwelling and enjoyment for a time}, he said: It is his dwelling on earth, his dwelling in the womb, and his dwelling beneath the earth until he passes to Paradise or to Hell. Then he looked and said: A Garden whose width is the heavens and the earth - he said: Seven heavens and seven earths, joined together as garments are joined to one another. He said: This is its width, and no one can describe its length."
"899","Verse (105), His saying, Exalted is He: {And thus We diversify the signs, that they may say: You have studied, and that We may make it clear to a people who know}. 899 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, he said: I heard Sa'id ibn Jubayr reporting from Ibn 'Abbas that he used to recite {darasta} (you studied together / you disputed) with an alif, he said: You recited mutually."
"900","900 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from 'Amr ibn Kaysan, he said: I heard Ibn 'Abbas saying: {darasta} means: you disputed and recited."
"901","901 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr, he heard Ibn al-Zubayr saying: Our children here say {darasta}, but it is only {darasta}; and they recite {hami'ah} (muddy), but it is only {hamiyah} (hot); and they recite {wa harrama} (and he forbade), but it is only (haram - forbidden); and Ibn 'Abbas used to differ with him in all of them."
"902","902 - Sa'id narrated, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Abu Ishaq, from a man of Banu Tamim, he said: I asked Ibn 'Abbas about His saying, Mighty and Majestic, {darasta}, he said: You read and learned."
"903","903 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from a man, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Tamimi, from Ibn 'Abbas, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {darasta}, he said: You read and learned."
"904","904 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from a man, from Mujahid, he said: You read, and they read to you."
"905","905 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, that he used to say {darasta}, he said: You read and learned."
"906","906 - Sa'id narrated, he said: 'Abbad ibn 'Abbad al-Muhallabi narrated to us, he said: al-Zubayr ibn al-Khirrit narrated to us, from 'Ikrimah, that he used to recite {darasta}, saying: You studied with the People of the Book; you recited mutually with them."
"907","907 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Juwaybir narrated to us, from al-Dahhak - like the hadith of Abu Bishr."
"908","908 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from 'Abbad ibn Rashid, from al-Hasan, that he used to recite (darrasta) with doubling (shaddah)."
"909","909 - Sa'id narrated, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Abu Ishaq, he said: It is the recitation of 'Abdullah (darrasta)."
"910","Verses (119-121), His saying, Exalted is He: {And why should you not eat of that over which the name of Allah has been mentioned, when He has detailed for you what He forbade you, except what you are compelled to} up to His saying, Exalted is He: {And do not eat of that over which the name of Allah has not been mentioned, for it is wickedness}. 910 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard 'Atiyyah al-'Awfi reciting: {And He has detailed for you what He forbade you}."
"911","911 - Sa'id narrated, he said: 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Salih informed me, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, passed by the butchers and said: Who slaughters for you? They said: This one. He said: You slaughter for these? He said: Yes. He said: Tell me about such-and-such prayer - and he did not know it, so he struck him and expelled him from the market, and struck the butchers, saying: One like this slaughters for you, while Allah says: {And do not eat of that over which the name of Allah has not been mentioned}!"
"912","912 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, regarding a man who slaughters and forgets to pronounce the name, he said: He disliked it, but did not say it is unlawful."
"913","913 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, regarding a man who slaughters and forgets to pronounce the name, he said: He may eat."
"914","914 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from 'Ayn, from Ibn 'Abbas, regarding one who slaughters and forgets the invocation, he said: The Muslim contains the name of Allah in him, even if he did not mention the invocation."
"915","915 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Khalid ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from 'Ata, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said: Whoever slaughters and forgets to pronounce the name, let him mention the name of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, over it and eat, and not leave it for Satan, if he slaughtered upon the natural disposition."
"916","916 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Khalid ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Sumay', from Malik ibn 'Umayr, that Walan passed by a mule of his, he said: I reached the house, he said: And there was a slaughtered sheep, and he said to some women around it: Who slaughtered it? They said: So-and-so, your slave, slaughtered it. He said: By Allah, my slave does not pray! They said: But we taught him and he pronounced the name. So I returned as I was and came to Ibn Mas'ud and informed him of the women's teaching him the invocation, and he said: Eat."
"917","Verse (122), His saying, Exalted is He: {Is one who was dead and We gave him life and made for him a light by which he walks among people, like one whose likeness is in darknesses from which he cannot emerge}. 917 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {Is one who was dead and We gave him life} - saying: Is one who was a disbeliever and We guided him."
"918","Verse (125), His saying, Exalted is He: {So whoever Allah wills to guide, He opens his breast to Islam; and whoever He wills to misguide, He makes his breast tight and constricted, as though he were climbing into the sky}. 918 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Abi Karimah, from 'Abdullah ibn Miswar - he was of the descendants of Ja'far ibn Abi Talib - he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited this verse: {So whoever Allah wills to guide, He opens his breast to Islam}. They said: Is there a knowledge by which that is known? He said: Yes; when light enters the heart it widens and expands. They said: Is there a knowledge by which that is known? He said: Yes: turning to the abode of eternity, keeping aloof from the abode of delusion, and preparing for death before death descends."
"919","Verse (128), His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {And the Day He gathers them all: O company of jinn, you have taken many of mankind; and their allies among mankind will say: Our Lord, we enjoyed one another, and we reached our term which You appointed for us}. 919 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Isma'il ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Musa ibn 'Ubaydah, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {Our Lord, we enjoyed one another} - he said: Companionship; {and we reached our term which You appointed for us} - he said: Death."
"920","Verse (133), His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {And your Lord is Self-Sufficient, Possessor of mercy; if He wills He can remove you and bring after you what He wills, as He produced you from the offspring of other people}. 920 - Sa'id narrated, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Kharijah ibn Zayd, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that he used to recite {as He produced you from the offspring of other people}."
"921","Verse (138), His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {And they say: These cattle and tillage are forbidden; none shall eat them except whom we will, by their claim}. 921 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid, he heard Ibn al-Zubayr reciting: {cattle and tillage forbidden}."
"922","Verse (141), His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {And He it is who produced gardens, trellised} up to His saying, Exalted is He: {Eat of its fruit when it bears fruit, and pay its due on the day of its harvest}. 922 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {And pay its due on the day of its harvest} - he said: At sowing he gives a handful, at harvest he gives a handful, and he leaves them to follow the traces of the reaping."
"923","923 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Jarir ibn 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {And pay its due on the day of its harvest} - he said: When you reap and the poor are present, throw to them of the ears; when you thresh it and heap it and the poor are present, throw to them of it; when you tread it and winnow it and the poor are present, throw to them of it; when you winnow it, gather it and know its measure, set aside its zakat; when the dates ripen and the poor are present, throw to them of the scattered and unripe dates; when you cut them and the poor are present, throw to them of it; and when you gather it and know its measure, set aside its zakat."
"924","924 - Sa'id narrated, he said: 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ja'far, from his father, from 'Ali ibn al-Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade harvesting by night and cutting dates by night."
"925","925 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {And pay its due on the day of its harvest} - he said: Apart from zakat."
"926","926 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Khalid ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, from Bayan, from al-Sha'bi, he said: In wealth there is indeed a right apart from zakat."
"927","927 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Shibak, from Ibrahim, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {And pay its due on the day of its harvest} - he said: It was abrogated by zakat: the tenth and half the tenth."
"928","928 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn 'Abbas, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {And pay its due on the day of its harvest} - he said: The tenth and half the tenth."
"929","929 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Ata, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {And pay its due on the day of its harvest} - he said: A small thing apart from the obligatory zakat; and Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib used to say: It is the obligatory zakat."
"930","930 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said: Whoever pays the zakat of his wealth, there is no sin upon him if he does not give further charity."
"931","931 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu Shihab narrated to us, from Abu 'Abdullah al-Thaqafi, from Abu Ja'far, from Muhammad ibn 'Ali, that he heard 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: Allah has imposed upon the rich in their wealth enough to suffice their poor; if they hunger, go naked or suffer hardship, it is due to the withholding of the rich; and it is binding upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic, to reckon them on the Day of Resurrection and punish them for it."
"932","Verse (142), His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {And of cattle, beasts of burden and small ones; eat of what Allah has provided you}. 932 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated to us - Mughirah informed us - from Ibrahim, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {beasts of burden and small ones (farsh)} - he said: The burden-bearers are what is ridden and carried upon of camels, and the farsh are the small ones."
"933","Verse (145), His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {Say: I find not in what is revealed to me anything forbidden to an eater to eat, except carrion, or flowing blood, or the flesh of swine} - the verse. 933 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from 'Ikrimah, he said: Were it not for this verse {or blood} - the Muslims would have followed from the veins what the Jews follow thereof."
"934","Verse (151), His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {And do not approach indecencies, what is apparent of them and what is hidden}. 934 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Qays, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {My Lord has only forbidden indecencies, what is apparent of them and what is hidden} - he said: What was apparent: they used to circumambulate the House naked; and what was hidden: adultery."
"935","Verse (153), His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {And that this is My straight path, so follow it, and do not follow ways, lest they separate you from His way}. 935 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drew a line for us and said: This is the way of Allah; then he drew lines to its right and its left and said: And these are ways; upon each way is a devil calling to it. Then he recited: {And that this is My straight path, so follow it, and do not follow ways, lest they separate you from His way}."
"936","Verse (158), His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {Do they await but that the angels come to them, or your Lord comes, or some of the signs of your Lord come? The day some of the signs of your Lord come, no soul shall benefit from its faith if it had not believed before, or earned good in its faith}. 936 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us, from Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab, from Abu al-'Aliyah, he said: A man recited in his presence this verse (the day some of the signs of your Lord come, no soul shall benefit from its faith) and he did not correct him, though he would not correct anyone's recitation; then he himself said: {The day some of the signs of your Lord come, no soul shall benefit from its faith if it had not believed before}. I mentioned this hadith to Ibrahim, and he said: I think your companion has heard a report, or heard that whoever disbelieves in a letter of it has disbelieved in all of it."
"937","937 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, he said: Ash'ath ibn Sulaym narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah said: Will they not hear that repentance is extended so long as the sun has not risen from the west?"
"938","938 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {no soul shall benefit from its faith} - he said: The rising of the sun from the west."
"939","939 - Sa'id narrated, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Ibn Mas'ud, regarding His saying: {The day some of the signs of your Lord come} - he said: The rising of the sun from the west."
"940","940 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, he said: I came to Safwan ibn 'Assal al-Muradi, and he said to me: What brought you? I said: Seeking knowledge. He said: It has reached me that the angels lower their wings for the seeker of knowledge, pleased with what he does. I said: Something concerning wiping over the leather socks troubled my mind; have you retained anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about it? He said: Yes; when we traveled we were commanded not to remove our socks for three (days), except from major impurity, but for stool, urine and sleep (we wiped). I said: Have you retained anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about love? He said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on one of his journeys, when a man at the rear of the people called him with a loud voice - a coarse, uncouth Bedouin - saying to him: O Muhammad! The people said to him: Hush; you have been forbidden this! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) answered him in a voice like his: Come here. He said to him: A man loves a people but has not yet joined them? He said: He is with whom he loves. Zirr said: He kept narrating to me until he narrated to me that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, placed in the west a gate whose width is seventy years (journey) for repentance; it is not closed so long as the sun has not risen from its direction. That is His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {The day some of the signs of your Lord come} up to His saying: {Indeed we are waiting}."
"941","Verse (159), His saying, Exalted is He: {Indeed those who divided their religion and became sects - you are not of them in anything; their affair is only with Allah, then He will inform them of what they used to do}. 941 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hibban ibn 'Ali narrated to us, from Mujalid ibn Sa'id, he said: Murrah al-Hamdani wept, and it was said to him: What makes you weep? He said: I fear that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, may be free of you; I hear Allah saying: {Indeed those who divided their religion and became sects - you are not of them in anything} - and I fear that Allah may not be of us in anything."
"942","Chapter: Commentary on Surat al-A'raf. Commentary on Surat al-A'raf. Verses (8 and 9), His saying, Exalted is He: {And the weighing that Day is truth; so those whose scales are heavy - they are the successful. And those whose scales are light - they are the ones who lost themselves for wronging Our signs}. 942 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn al-Marzuban, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Abdullah ibn Sabit, he said: When word reached the people that Abu Bakr intended to appoint 'Umar as successor, they said: What will he say to his Lord when he meets Him? He appointed over us a harsh, stern man, while he cannot do anything (now)! How then if he gains power? That reached Abu Bakr, and he said: Do you frighten me with my Lord? I say: I appointed the best of your people. Then he sent for 'Umar and said: Allah has a deed of the night He does not accept by day, and a deed of the day He does not accept by night; and know that no supererogatory act will be accepted until the obligatory is performed. Have you not seen that Allah mentioned the people of Paradise and mentioned them by their best deeds, since He overlooked evil, until the speaker says: How can my deed reach this? Have you not seen that when Allah mentioned the people of Hell, He mentioned them by their worst deeds, since He rejected their good and it was not accepted from them, until the speaker says: My deed is better than this? Have you not seen that Allah sent down hope and fear, so that the believer may fear and act, and may hope and not throw himself into destruction? Have you not seen that those whose scales are heavy on the Day of Resurrection, their scales grew heavy by following truth and abandoning falsehood, and that weighed upon them; and it is fitting for a scale in which nothing but truth is placed to be heavy? Have you not seen that the scales of those whose scales are light were light only by following falsehood and abandoning truth, and it is fitting for a scale in which nothing but falsehood is placed to be light? Then he said: If you preserve my counsel, no absent thing will be dearer to you than death - and you shall surely meet it! And if you waste my counsel, no absent thing will be more hateful to you than death - and you cannot escape it."
"943","Verse (24), His saying, Exalted is He: {He said: Descend, some of you enemies to others; and for you on earth is a dwelling and enjoyment for a time}. 943 - Sa'id narrated, he said: al-Hasan ibn Yazid narrated to us, from al-Suddi, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {Descend, some of you enemies to others; and for you on earth is a dwelling and enjoyment for a time} - he said: Adam and Hawwa'; and the snake - wherever the son of Adam finds it, he kills it, and wherever it finds the son of Adam, it seizes his arm."
"944","Verse (28), His saying, Exalted is He: {And when they commit an indecency, they say: We found our fathers upon it, and Allah commanded us with it. Say: Allah does not command indecency; do you say about Allah what you do not know}. 944 - Sa'id narrated - Jarir narrated to us - from Mansur, from Mujahid, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {And when they commit an indecency, they say: We found our fathers upon it, and Allah commanded us with it} - he said: They used to circumambulate the House naked."
"945","Verse (30), His saying, Exalted is He: {A party He guided, and upon a party straying was decreed; they took devils as allies besides Allah, thinking themselves guided}. 945 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from 'Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from one who heard Ibn 'Abbas mention the Qadariyyah, saying: May Allah fight them! Has not Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: {As He began you, you shall return. A party He guided, and upon a party straying was decreed}?"
"946","Verse (31), His saying, Exalted is He: {O children of Adam, take your adornment at every mosque; eat and drink, but do not waste; He does not love the wasteful}. 946 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {Take your adornment at every mosque} - he said: They used to circumambulate the House naked, so they were commanded to wear their garments."
"947","947 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr, from Tawus, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {Take your adornment at every mosque} - he said: Garments."
"948","Verse (40), His saying, Exalted is He: {Indeed those who denied Our signs and were arrogant toward them - the gates of heaven shall not be opened for them, nor shall they enter Paradise until the camel passes through the eye of the needle}. 948 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from Ibn Mas'ud, that he used to recite {until the camel (al-jamal) passes}; he said: The husband of the she-camel."
"949","949 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas, that he used to recite (until the thick rope - al-jummal - passes); he said: The thick ropes of ships, these cables."
"950","950 - Sa'id narrated, he said: 'Amr ibn Thabit narrated to us, from his father, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said: He used to recite (until the thick rope - al-jummal - passes); he said: The ropes of ships."
"951","951 - Sa'id narrated, he said: 'Amr ibn Thabit narrated to us, from his father, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: The husband of the she-camel."
"952","952 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Khalid ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that he used to recite (al-jummal - the thick rope)."
"953","953 - Sa'id narrated, he said: 'Umar ibn Salim al-Aftas narrated to us, from his father, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, that he used to recite (al-jummal), meaning a thick ship's rope."
"954","Verses (46-50), His saying, Exalted is He: {And between them is a veil, and upon the heights are men who know each by their marks} up to His saying, Exalted is He: {and they denied Our signs}. 954 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Shibl, from 'Amr ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Muzani, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the companions of the Heights (al-A'raf) and said: They are a people killed in the way of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, in disobedience to their parents; disobedience to their parents barred them from entering Paradise, and their being killed in the way of Allah barred them from entering Hell."
"955","955 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Husayn, from al-Sha'bi, from Hudhayfah, he said: The companions of the Heights are a people whose good deeds fell short of admitting them to Paradise, while their evils exceeded admitting them (to Hell); they are upon a wall between Paradise and Hell; they have not entered it, yet they hope."
"956","956 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Khalid ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, from Husayn, from al-Sha'bi, from Hudhayfah, he said: The companions of the Heights are a people whose evils kept them from Paradise and whose good deeds carried them past Hell; they were placed there until judgment is passed among people."
"957","957 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid, he heard Ibn 'Abbas asked about al-A'raf, he said: It is the elevated thing."
"958","958 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, from his father, he said: Abu Mijlaz informed me, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {And upon the heights are men who know each by their marks} - he said: The Heights is an elevated place, upon it are men of the angels who know the people of Paradise by their marks and the people of Hell by their marks. {And they called to the companions of Paradise: Peace be upon you; they have not entered it, yet they hope} to enter it; {and when their sight is turned} - he said: the sight of the people of Paradise, toward the companions of the Fire - {they say: Our Lord, place us not with the wrongdoing people. And the companions of the Heights called to men} of the disbelievers {whom they know by their marks, saying: Of no avail to you were your gathering and your arrogance. Are these they whom you swore Allah would not grant mercy? Enter Paradise; no fear upon you, nor shall you grieve} - this is when they entered it."
"959","Verse (127), His saying, Exalted is He: {And the chiefs of Pharaoh's people said: Will you leave Musa and his people to corrupt the land, while he abandons you and your gods}. 959 - Sa'id narrated, he said: 'Amr ibn Hasan narrated to us, from Ibn 'Abbas, that he used to recite: (while he abandons you and your worship - wa ilahataka). He said: Pharaoh is worshipped and does not worship."
"960","Verse (143), His saying, Exalted is He: {And when Musa came to Our appointed time and his Lord spoke to him, he said: My Lord, show me, that I may look at You} up to His saying, Exalted is He: {and I am the first of the believers}. 960 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Humayd al-A'raj, from 'Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The day Allah spoke to Musa, peace be upon him, he wore a woolen cloak, a woolen outer garment, woolen trousers, a woolen cap, and sandals of untanned donkey hide."
"961","961 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: 'Umar ibn Hamzah al-'Umari narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi saying: It was said to Musa, peace be upon him: To what among creation did you liken the speech of your Lord, Mighty and Majestic? He said: Thunder. 'Umar said: A man said: Muhammad said: Still thunder."
"962","962 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, he said: I heard al-Rabi' ibn Khuthaym reciting {He made it level (dakka')} with lengthening (madd)."
"963","Verse (145), His saying, Exalted is He: {And We wrote for him in the Tablets} up to His saying, Exalted is He: {I shall show you the abode of the corrupt}. 963 - Sa'id narrated, he said: 'Amr ibn Thabit narrated to us, from his father, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {I shall show you the abode of the corrupt} - he said: It was raised for Musa until he looked at it."
"964","Verses (156 and 157), His saying, Exalted is He: {And ordain for us good in this world and in the Hereafter; we have turned to You} up to His saying, Exalted is He: {those are the successful}. 964 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Khalid narrated to us, from Abu al-'Uryan, he said: Ibn 'Abbas said regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {And ordain for us good in this world and in the Hereafter; we have turned to You} - he said: Musa was not granted it. {He said: My punishment - I afflict with it whom I will, and My mercy embraces everything} up to His saying: {those are the successful}."
"965","965 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Qays, from Mujahid, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {And He removes from them their burden} - he said: Covenants that were upon them."
"966","Verse (169), His saying, Exalted is He: {Then there succeeded after them successors who inherited the Book, taking the fleeting goods of this low life and saying: We shall be forgiven} - the verse. 966 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Fudayl ibn 'Iyad narrated to us, from Mansur, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {Taking the fleeting goods of this low life and saying: We shall be forgiven} - he said: They commit sins and say: We shall be forgiven."
"967","Verse (172), His saying, Exalted is He: {And when your Lord took from the children of Adam, from their loins, their offspring, and made them testify about themselves: Am I not your Lord? They said: Yes, we testify}. 967 - Sa'id narrated, he said: 'Attab ibn Bashir narrated to us, he said: Khusayf narrated to us, from Mujahid and Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {And when your Lord took from the children of Adam, from their loins} - he said: He took from all the prophets before they were created. He said: He took the sperm-drops from the loins of Adam, and saw among them a sperm-drop gleaming. He said: My Lord, which of my sons is this? He said: This is your son Dawud. He said: My Lord, how much did You assign him? He said: Sixty years. He said: You made it little for him. He said: Then give him of your years, for I assigned you a thousand years - so he gave him forty years. When Adam's term came, he said: My Lord, did You not assign me a thousand years? Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: Did you not assign of your years forty years to Dawud? At that point Allah, Mighty and Majestic, commanded writing, witnesses and proof."
"968","968 - Sa'id narrated, he said: 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Sa'd informed me, from Shaybah ibn Nisah, he said: I asked Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib about coitus interruptus ('azl), and he said: When Allah, Mighty and Majestic, created Adam, He honored him with an honor He granted none of His creation: He showed him who would come from his loins until the Day of Resurrection; and if it be of what Allah showed him, it shall be, so it is no harm upon you not to do it."
"969","969 - Sa'id narrated, he said: 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Rabi'ah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Ibn Muhayriz, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked about coitus interruptus, and he said: It is no harm upon you not to do it; if it be of what Allah took the covenant from, though it were upon a rock, He would breathe the soul into it."
"970","Verse (187), His saying, Exalted is He: {They ask you about the Hour, when it shall come to pass} up to His saying, Exalted is He: {They ask you as though you were well-informed about it; say: Its knowledge is only with Allah}. 970 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, he said: Ibn 'Abbas used to recite (as though you were well-informed about it - hafiyyun biha)."
"971","971 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Mujahid, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {as though you were well-informed about it} - saying: As though you were affectionate to them, so they ask you about the Hour."
"972","Verses (189 and 190), His saying, Exalted is He: {He it is who created you from a single soul and made from it its mate, that he might dwell with her; then when he covered her, she bore a light burden and carried on with it; then when she grew heavy, they called upon Allah their Lord: If You give us a righteous one, we shall surely be of the thankful. Then when He gave them a righteous one, they set up partners for Him in what He gave them; exalted is Allah above what they associate}. 972 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, he said: Ibn 'Abbas used to recite: (she bore a light burden and continued with it - fastamarrat bihi)."
"973","973 - Sa'id narrated, he said: 'Attab ibn Bashir narrated to us, he said: Khusayf narrated to us, from Mujahid and Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {Then when she grew heavy, they called upon Allah their Lord: If You give us a righteous one, we shall surely be of the thankful. Then when He gave them a righteous one, they set up partners for Him in what He gave them} - he said: When Hawwa' became pregnant, Iblis came to her and said: I am the one who expelled you both from Paradise; if you do not obey me, I shall give your son two horns that will split your belly, or I shall bring him out dead! So it was decreed that he came out dead. Then she became pregnant a second time, and he said to her like his saying; Hawwa' said to him: Tell me what you want me to obey you in? He said: Name him 'Abd al-Harith - so she did, and he came out sound by Allah's permission. That is His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {They set up partners for Him in what He gave them}. And 'Ikrimah said: He did not single out Adam with it, but made it general for all people after Adam."
"974","Verse (199), His saying, Exalted is He: {Take pardon, command what is right, and turn away from the ignorant}. 974 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {Take pardon, command what is right, and turn away from the ignorant} - he said: He was commanded only to take of their manners and deeds."
"975","975 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, from Wahb ibn Kaysan, he said: I heard Ibn al-Zubayr saying upon the pulpit: {Take pardon, command what is right, and turn away from the ignorant}; by Allah, He commanded it only that we take of people's manners; by Allah, I shall surely take it of them so long as I accompany them."
"976","Verse (204), His saying, Exalted is He: {And when the Qur'an is recited, listen to it and be silent, that you may receive mercy}. 976 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: al-'Awwam narrated to us, from Mujahid, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {And when the Qur'an is recited, listen to it and be silent} - he said: During the sermon on Friday."
"977","977 - Sa'id narrated, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Mansur, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Hurrah, from Mujahid, he said: In prayer and the sermon."
"978","978 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b, he said: They used to catch up from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): when he recited something, they recited along with him, until this verse in al-A'raf was revealed: {And when the Qur'an is recited, listen to it and be silent}."
"979","979 - Sa'id narrated, he said: 'Awn ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: I heard Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah saying: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed this verse {And when the Qur'an is recited, listen to it and be silent} - concerning prayer; people used to talk in prayer, and the storytellers applied it to storytelling."
"980","980 - Sa'id narrated, he said: 'Awn ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: I heard Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah saying - I asked al-Hasan: Is reciting in a mushaf dearer to you, or sitting with a storyteller? He said: Recite in your mushaf. I said: Visiting a sick person is dearer to you, or sitting with a storyteller? He said: Visit your sick. I said: Escorting a funeral is dearer to you, or sitting with a storyteller? He said: Escort your funeral. I said: A man sought my help for a need - is it dearer to you that I go with him, or sit with a storyteller? He said: Go for your brother's need - until he made it the best of idle sittings."
"981","981 - Sa'id narrated, he said: 'Awn ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: I heard Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah saying: A merchant who brings us food is dearer to me than a storyteller between two. He said: And I heard Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah saying: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said to women: {And remain in your houses}, while the storytellers command them to go out."
"982","Chapter: Commentary on Surat al-Anfal. Commentary on Surat al-Anfal. Verse (1), His saying, Exalted is He: {They ask you about the spoils; say: The spoils belong to Allah and the Messenger; so fear Allah, set right what is between you, and obey Allah and His Messenger if you are believers}. 982 - Sa'id narrated, he said: 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Ayyash ibn Abi Rabi'ah, from Sulayman ibn Musa al-Ashdaq, from Makhul, from Abu Sallam al-Bahili, from Abu Umamah al-Bahili, from 'Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to Badr and met the enemy there; when Allah routed them, a party of the Muslims followed them, killing them; a party surrounded the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and a party took possession of the plunder and the camp. When those who pursued the enemy returned, they said: The extra share is ours; we pursued the enemy, and through us Allah, Mighty and Majestic, expelled and routed them. Those who surrounded the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are no more entitled to it than we; it is rather ours - we surrounded the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) lest the enemy catch him unawares! Those who took possession of the plunder and camp said: You are no more entitled to it than we; it is rather ours - we took possession of it and secured it. So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed to His Messenger: {They ask you about the spoils; say: The spoils belong to Allah and the Messenger; so fear Allah, set right what is between you} - the verse. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided it among them evenly; the Messenger of Allah would grant them extra shares of a fourth at the outset, and a third upon return. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a hair from a camel's back and said: Nothing of the fay' is lawful to me to the measure of this hair except the fifth, and the fifth is returned to you; so return the needle and thread, beware of misappropriation, for it is a disgrace for its people on the Day of Resurrection; and upon you is jihad, for it is a gate of Paradise by which Allah removes grief and sorrow. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked the extra share (nafal) and said: The strong of the people return it to their weak."
"983","983 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from Muhammad ibn 'Ubaydullah al-Thaqafi, from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, he said: On the day of Badr I killed Sa'id ibn al-'As and took his sword, which was called Dhu al-Katifah; I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Go and cast it into the collection. I went, with in me what none but Allah, Mighty and Majestic, knows, of killing my brother and taking my spoil; I had barely passed him when Surat al-Anfal was revealed, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Go and take your sword."
"984","984 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: I said to Ibn 'Abbas: Surat al-Anfal? He said: It was revealed concerning the people of Badr."
"985","Verses (15-16), His saying, Exalted is He: {O you who believe, when you meet the disbelievers advancing, do not turn them your backs. Whoever turns them his back that day, except maneuvering for battle or joining a company, has incurred wrath from Allah, and his abode is Hell - an evil destination}. 985 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Khalid ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ibn 'Umar, he said: We met the enemy, and the Muslims swerved aside; I was among those who swerved. We came to Madinah and presented ourselves to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he came out to prayer, saying: O Messenger of Allah, we are the fleers! He said: Rather you are the returners to fight; I am your company."
"986","986 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, he said: 'Umar said: I am the company of every Muslim."
"987","Verse (27), His saying, Exalted is He: {O you who believe, do not betray Allah and the Messenger, nor betray your trusts while you know}. 987 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Khalid, he said: I heard 'Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah saying in the mosque of Kufah: This verse was revealed: {Do not betray Allah and the Messenger} - he said: The Banu Qurayzah asked Abu Lubabah ibn 'Abd al-Mundhir, on the day of Qurayzah: What is this matter? And he pointed to his throat, meaning: Slaughter. So this verse was revealed. He said: Sufyan said: Abu Lubabah said: My feet did not move until I knew I had betrayed Allah and His Messenger."
"988","988 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Ka'b ibn Malik, that Abu Lubabah ibn 'Abd al-Mundhir - or Ka'b ibn Malik - said: O Messenger of Allah, part of my repentance is to divest myself of my wealth and abandon my house in which I committed the sin! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A third of that suffices you."
"989","Verse (29), His saying, Exalted is He: {O you who believe, if you fear Allah, He will grant you a criterion} - the verse. 989 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {If you fear Allah, He will grant you a criterion} - an escape."
"990","Verse (32), His saying, Exalted is He: {And when they said: O Allah, if this is the truth from You, rain upon us stones from the sky} - the verse. 990 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {If this is the truth from You, rain upon us stones from the sky} - he said: It was revealed concerning al-Nadr ibn al-Harith."
"991","Verses (33-34), His saying, Exalted is He: {And Allah would not punish them while you are among them, nor would Allah punish them while they seek forgiveness. But what ails them that Allah should not punish them, while they bar from the Sacred Mosque} - the verse. 991 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Khalid ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, from Husayn, from Abu Malik, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {And Allah would not punish them while you are among them, nor would Allah punish them while they seek forgiveness}, he said: This is for the Muslims. {But what ails them that Allah should not punish them}, he said: This is for the polytheists."
"992","(40), His saying, Exalted is He: {And if they turn away, know that Allah is your Protector - an excellent Protector and excellent Helper}. 992 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, he said: 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud led us in the last evening prayer, opening al-Anfal; he recited until he reached {an excellent Protector and excellent Helper} - then bowed; then he stood and recited another surah in the second rak'ah."
"993","Verse (41), His saying, Exalted is He: {And know that whatever you take as spoils, a fifth of it belongs to Allah, the Messenger and near kin} up to His saying, Exalted is He: {the day of criterion, the day the two hosts met; and Allah is Able over everything}. 993 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah narrated to us, from Ibrahim, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {And know that whatever you take as spoils, a fifth of it belongs to Allah and the Messenger} - he said: The fifth is divided into five fifths; the fifth of Allah and the Messenger is one, and the rest is divided among the others."
"994","994 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Abi 'A'ishah, he said: I asked Yahya ibn al-Jazzar about the share of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of the fifth, he said: A fifth of the fifth."
"995","995 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Suwayd ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, from Husayn, from Ibrahim, from Ibn Mas'ud, regarding His saying: {the day of criterion, the day the two hosts met} - he said: The night of Badr was seventeen nights past of the month of Ramadan."
"996","996 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: Seek Laylat al-Qadr on the seventeenth past of Ramadan, the morning of the day of Badr, the day of criterion, the day the two hosts met, and on the twenty-first and twenty-third; for it occurs only on an odd night."
"997","Verse (50), His saying, Exalted is He: {And if you could see when the angels take the disbelievers, striking their faces and their backs: Taste the punishment of burning}. 997 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Kathir, he said: Mujahid said to me: Do you know what His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {striking their faces and their backs} is? I said: What is it? He said: And their posteriors - but Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is Generous and uses euphemism."
"998","Verse (55), His saying, Exalted is He: {Indeed the worst of creatures with Allah are those who disbelieved, so they do not believe}. 998 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {Indeed the worst of creatures with Allah are those who disbelieved, so they do not believe} to the end of the verse, he said: Six men of the Jews. Ayyub said: He named them, among them Ibn Tabut."
"999","Verse (60), His saying, Exalted is He: {And prepare for them what you can of strength} - the verse. 999 - Sa'id narrated, he said: 'Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Abu 'Ali al-Hamdani, that he heard 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying regarding {And prepare for them what you can of strength}: Verily strength is archery; verily strength is archery - he said it three times."
"1000","Verse (65), His saying, Exalted is He: {O Prophet, urge the believers to fight} up to His saying, Exalted is He: {because they are a people who do not understand}. 1000 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, he said: Ibn 'Abbas said regarding {O Prophet, urge the believers to fight; if there be twenty steadfast among you, they shall overcome two hundred} - he said: It was prescribed upon them that twenty not flee from two hundred; then Allah lightened it for them, saying: Now Allah has lightened for you, knowing there is weakness in you - so a hundred ought not flee from two hundred."
"1001","1001 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan and Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from 'Ata, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said: If a man flees from two men, he has fled; if he flees from three, he has not fled."
"1002","Verse (68), His saying, Exalted is He: {Had it not been for a prior decree from Allah, a great punishment would have touched you for what you took}. 1002 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, he said regarding {Had it not been for a prior decree from Allah}: that I permitted you the spoils in My knowledge - a great punishment would have touched you for what you took of captives - meaning the day of Badr."
"1003","Chapter: Commentary on Surat al-Tawbah. Commentary on Surat al-Tawbah. 1003 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym, Fudayl ibn 'Iyad and Khalid ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, from Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Abu 'Atiyyah al-Hamdani, he said: 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, wrote: Learn Surat Bara'ah, teach your women Surat al-Nur, and adorn them with silver."
"1004","1004 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: I said to Ibn 'Abbas: Surat al-Tawbah? He said: Rather it is the Exposer; it kept being revealed - and of them, and of them - until they thought none of them would remain unmentioned in it."
"1005","Verse (2), His saying, Exalted is He: {So travel in the land for four months}. 1005 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani, from Zayd ibn Yuthay', he said: We asked 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: With what were you sent? He said: With four: that none but a believing soul shall enter Paradise; that no naked one shall circumambulate the House; that no Muslim and polytheist shall gather after this year of theirs in Hajj; whoever has a covenant, his covenant stands to its term, and whoever has no covenant, then four months."
"1006","Verse (3), His saying, Exalted is He: {And a proclamation from Allah and His Messenger to people on the day of the greater Hajj}. 1006 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaddad, he said: The greater Hajj is the day of sacrifice, and the lesser Hajj is 'Umrah."
"1007","1007 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr, he said: I went with Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman until we entered upon 'Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa; Abu Salamah asked him about the greater Hajj. He said: It is that in which sacrifice is made, the sacred state is ended, and hair is removed."
"1008","1008 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, he said: We asked 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, about the greater Hajj. He said: It is the day of sacrifice."
"1009","1009 - Sa'id narrated, he said: ... al-A'mash narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Sinan al-Asadi, he said: al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah addressed us upon a camel on the day of sacrifice, saying: Today is sacrifice, and today is the greater Hajj. [Flag: isnad garbled/truncated in source ('... al-A'mash')]."
"1010","Verse (18), His saying, Exalted is He: {Only he maintains the mosques of Allah who believes in Allah and the Last Day}. 1010 - Sa'id narrated, he said: 'Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Darraj Abu al-Samh, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: When you see a man frequenting the mosque, testify to his faith; Allah, Mighty Speaker, said: {Only he maintains the mosques of Allah who believes in Allah and the Last Day}."
"1011","Verse (28), His saying, Exalted is He: {O you who believe, the polytheists are impure, so let them not approach the Sacred Mosque after this year of theirs; and if you fear poverty, Allah shall enrich you of His bounty if He wills; Allah is Knowing, Wise}. 1011 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, he said: Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from 'Ikrimah, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {O you who believe, the polytheists are impure, so let them not approach the Sacred Mosque after this year of theirs; and if you fear poverty, Allah shall enrich you of His bounty if He wills; Allah is Knowing, Wise} - he said: The polytheists used to come to the House bringing food with them; so Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: {And if you fear poverty, Allah shall enrich you of His bounty if He wills}; and Allah sent down rain upon them, and their good multiplied, until the polytheists left them."
"1012","Verse (31), His saying, Exalted is He: {They took their rabbis and monks as lords besides Allah, and the Messiah son of Maryam; yet they were commanded only to worship one God; there is no god but He; glory to Him above what they associate}. 1012 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: al-'Awwam ibn Hawshab narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, he said: Abu al-Bakhtari al-Ta'i narrated to me, he said: Hudhayfah said to me: Have you seen His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {They took their rabbis and monks as lords besides Allah} - Hudhayfah said: They did not pray to them, but whatever unlawful they made lawful for them, they deemed lawful; and whatever lawful they forbade them of unlawful, they forbade it - that is their lordship."
"1013","Verse (33), His saying, Exalted is He: {He it is who sent His Messenger with guidance and the religion of truth, to make it prevail over all religion, though the polytheists dislike it}. 1013 - Sa'id narrated, he said: 'Amr ibn Thabit narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Ja'far, from Jabir ibn 'Abdullah, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {to make it prevail over all religion} - he said: The emergence of 'Isa ibn Maryam, peace and blessings be upon him."
"1014","Verse (36), His saying, Exalted is He: {Indeed the number of months with Allah is twelve months in the Book of Allah, the day He created the heavens and the earth; of them four are sacred} - the verse. 1014 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-Kalbi, from Abu Salih, from Ibn 'Abbas, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {of them four are sacred} - he said: Muharram, Rajab, Dhu al-Qa'dah and Dhu al-Hijjah."
"1015","Verse (37), His saying, Exalted is He: {Postponement is an increase in disbelief, by which the disbelievers are led astray; they make it lawful one year and forbid it one year} - the verse. 1015 - Sa'id narrated, he said: Jarir ibn 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {Postponement is an increase in disbelief} - he said: Al-Nasi' was a man of Kinanah, a man of judgment among them; he would make Muharram in one year Safar, raiding in it and taking spoils, and in one year forbid it and not raid in it. That is His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {they make it lawful one year and forbid it one year}."
"1016","Verse (41), Allah the Most High's saying: {March forth, light or heavy, and strive with your wealth and your lives in the cause of Allah; that is better for you, if you only knew.} 1016 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Husayn, from Abu Malik, he said: The first thing revealed of Bara'ah after the first forty [verses] was: {March forth, light or heavy...} up to His saying: {if you only knew.}"
"1017","Verse (43), Allah the Most High's saying: {May Allah pardon you; why did you give them permission until it became clear to you who spoke the truth and you knew the liars?} 1017 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, he said: I heard 'Amr ibn Maymun al-Awdi say: Two things the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did without being commanded concerning them: his giving permission to the hypocrites, and his taking [ransom] from the captives - until Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down: {May Allah pardon you; why did you give them permission}, and: {It is not for a prophet to have captives.}"
"1018","1018 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mis'ar - or someone else - from 'Awn, he said: He informed him of the pardon before informing him of the fault."
"1019","1019 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Humayd, that he used to recite {captives (asra)}."
"1020","Verse (47), Allah the Most High's saying: {Had they gone forth with you, they would have added to you nothing but confusion, and would have hurried about among you seeking to cause you discord, and among you are listeners to them.} 1020 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Mujahid, regarding His saying, Majestic and Mighty: {and among you are listeners to them} - he said: Spies who are not hypocrites; among them are 'Abdullah ibn Abi Rifa'ah and Ibn Tabut."
"1021","Verse (60), Allah the Most High's saying: {Alms are only for the poor and the needy} up to His saying, the Most High: {and Allah is All-Knowing, All-Wise.} 1021 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Shihab narrated to us, from Hajjaj ibn Artah, from al-Minhal ibn 'Amr, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Hudhayfah, he said: These categories were named only so that they be known: {Alms are only for the poor and the needy, and those employed in them, and those whose hearts are reconciled, and for [freeing] necks, and the debtors, and in the cause of Allah, and the traveler} - whichever category of them you give to, it suffices you."
"1022","1022 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Muhajir Abu al-Hasan, he said: I came to Abu Wa'il alone, and he said: Return it and place it in its [proper] places. I said: What should I do with the share of those whose hearts are reconciled? He said: Return it upon the others."
"1023","1023 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Shihab ibn Khirash narrated to us, from Musa ibn Yazid al-Kindi, he said: Ibn Mas'ud used to teach a man to recite, and he recited: {Alms are only for the poor and the needy} - with qasr (without prolongation). So Ibn Mas'ud said: This is not how the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught it to me! He said: And how did he teach it to you, O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman? He said: He taught it to me {Alms are only for the poor and the needy} - and he prolonged it (with madd)."
"1024","1024 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: 'Umar ibn Nafi' narrated to us, from Abu Bakr al-'Absi, from 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him), regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {Alms are only for the poor and the needy} - he said: The poor (al-fuqara) are the chronically infirm (zamna) of the People of the Book."
"1025","Verse (74), Allah the Most High's saying: {And they resented nothing except that Allah and His Messenger enriched them of His bounty.} 1025 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from 'Ikrimah, he said: A man, a freedman (mawla) of Banu 'Adi ibn Ka'b, killed a man of the Ansar, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave judgment [in the case] for him, and concerning it was revealed: {And they resented nothing except that Allah and His Messenger enriched them of His bounty.}"
"1026","Verses (75-77), Allah the Most High's saying: {And among them are those who covenanted with Allah: If He gives us of His bounty, we will surely give charity} up to His saying, the Most High: {and for what they used to lie.} 1026 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from 'Umarah ibn 'Umayr, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, he said: 'Abdullah said: Recognize the hypocrites by three things: when he speaks he lies, when he promises he breaks it, and when he covenants he betrays. So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down in confirmation of that: {And among them are those who covenanted with Allah: If He gives us of His bounty, we will surely give charity}, to the end of the verse."
"1027","Verse (79), Allah the Most High's saying: {Those who criticize the voluntary givers among the believers in charities, and those who find nothing but their striving.} 1027 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from 'Isa ibn Mughirah, from al-Sha'bi, that he used to recite: {and those who find nothing but their juhd}. He said: Al-juhd (with damma) is regarding livelihood, and al-juhd means exertion (al-jahd)."
"1028","Verse (82), Allah the Most High's saying: {So let them laugh a little and weep much, as recompense for what they used to earn.} 1028 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Sumay', from Abu Razin, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {So let them laugh a little and weep much} - he said: This world is little, so let them laugh therein as much as they wish; then when they pass on to the Hereafter, they will weep a weeping that does not cease - and that is the much."
"1029","Verse (87), Allah the Most High's saying: {They were content to be with those left behind, and their hearts were sealed, so they do not understand.} 1029 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, [transmitting] by reading [to him], from Mujahid, he said: {Al-khawalif} are the women."
"1030","Verse (90), Allah the Most High's saying: {And there came the excuse-makers among the Bedouins that permission be given them} - the verse. 1030 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Humayd al-A'raj, from Mujahid, that he used to recite: {And there came the excuse-makers (al-mu'adhdhirun).}"
"1031","Verse (92), Allah the Most High's saying: {Nor upon those who, when they came to you that you carry them, you said: I find nothing to carry you upon - they turned back with their eyes overflowing with tears} - the verse. 1031 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, [transmitting] by reading [to him], from Mujahid, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {Nor upon those who, when they came to you that you carry them, you said: I find nothing to carry you upon - they turned back with their eyes overflowing with tears} - he said: They are Banu Muqarrin of Muzaynah."
"1032","1032 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out to Tabuk, he said: None shall set out with us except one well-provisioned. So a man set out upon a refractory young camel of his, and it threw him and broke his neck, and he died. People began saying: A martyr, a martyr! So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Bilal to proclaim among the people that none shall enter Paradise except a believing soul, and no disobedient one shall enter it. Mujahid said: We never heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a hadith more severe than this; and of his hadith: Sa'd was indeed squeezed a squeezing [in the grave]."
"1033","Verse (100), Allah the Most High's saying: {And the foremost, the first of the Emigrants and the Helpers, and those who followed them in goodness} - the verse. 1033 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from al-Sha'bi, he said: The first Emigrants are those who witnessed the Pledge of al-Ridwan."
"1034","Verse (101), Allah the Most High's saying: {And among those around you of the Bedouins are hypocrites} up to His saying, the Most High: {We shall punish them twice; then they will be returned to a great punishment.} 1034 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Attab ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Mujahid, regarding His saying: {We shall punish them twice} - he said: They were punished with hunger twice."
"1035","Verse (108), Allah the Most High's saying: {Never stand therein; a mosque founded upon piety from the first day is more worthy that you stand therein} - the verse. 1035 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from Kharijah ibn Zayd, he said: The mosque founded upon piety - he said: That is the mosque of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1036","1036 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Abidah ibn Humayd narrated to us, from 'Ammar al-Duhni, he said: I entered the mosque of Quba to pray in it, then I turned to my right, and Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman saw me and said: Would you like to pray in the mosque founded upon piety from the first day?!"
"1037","Verses (113-115), Allah the Most High's saying: {It is not for the Prophet and those who believe to seek forgiveness for the polytheists} up to His saying, the Most High: {Indeed Allah is Knowing of all things.} 1037 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Sinan, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: A man came to Ibn 'Abbas and said: My father died a Christian. He said to him: Wash him, shroud him and embalm him, then bury him. Then he recited this verse: {It is not for the Prophet and those who believe to seek forgiveness for the polytheists, even if they be kin, after it has become clear to them that they are companions of Hell * And the seeking of forgiveness of Ibrahim for his father was only because of a promise he had made to him; but when it became clear to him that he was an enemy to Allah, he dissociated himself from him.} He said: When he died upon disbelief, it became clear to him that he was an enemy to Allah, so he dissociated himself from him."
"1038","1038 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, regarding His saying: {when it became clear to him} - he said: When he died."
"1039","1039 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Abu Sinan Dirar ibn Murrah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: A man came to Ibn 'Abbas and said to him: My father died a Christian. He said to him: Wash him, shroud him and embalm him, then bury him. Then he recited this verse: {It is not for the Prophet and those who believe} to the end of the verse."
"1040","1040 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Isma'il narrated to us, from 'Amir ibn Shaqiq, from Abu Wa'il, he said: My mother died a Christian, so I came to 'Umar ibn al-Khattab and said: My mother died a Christian. He said: Mount a riding beast and go in front of her funeral procession."
"1041","1041 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Najiyah ibn Ka'b, he said: 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: When Abu Talib died, I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, your misguided uncle has died! He said to me: Go and bury him, and do not do anything until you come to me. He said: So I went, buried him, and came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with traces of dust upon me, and he supplicated for me with supplications - it would not please me more to have in exchange for them all that is upon the face of the earth."
"1042","1042 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Yazid al-Asamm narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Suddi narrating from Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, from 'Ali, he said: When Abu Talib died, I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Your aged uncle has died! He said to me: Go and bury him, then do not do anything until you come to me. So I took a bath (ghusl) then came to him, and he supplicated for me with supplications - it would not please me more to have in exchange for them the red and the black camels. And 'Ali, when he washed the dead, would himself take ghusl."
"1043","1043 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from 'Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, he said: 'Abdullah was asked about al-awwah; he said: It is the one who supplicates much."
"1044","1044 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, he said: Abu al-'Ubaydayn said to 'Abdullah: Whom shall we ask if we do not ask you - what is al-awwah? He said: The merciful one."
"1045","Verse (118), Allah the Most High's saying: {And upon the three who were left behind, until when the earth closed upon them despite its vastness} - the verse. 1045 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Masruq, from 'Ikrimah, regarding His saying: {And upon the three who were left behind} - he said: Ka'b ibn Malik, Hilal ibn Umayyah, and Murarah ibn al-Rabi' - all of them of the Ansar."
"1046","1046 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir ibn 'Abdullah, he said: Ka'b ibn Malik, Hilal ibn Umayyah, and Murarah ibn Rabi' - all of them of the Ansar."
"1047","Verse (119), Allah the Most High's saying: {O you who believe, fear Allah and be with the truthful.} 1047 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Masruq, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, he said: 'Abdullah said: No lying is permissible, neither in earnest nor in jest; that is because Allah says: {O you who believe, fear Allah and be with the truthful.}"
"1048","1048 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu 'Ubaydah, from 'Abdullah, he said: No lying is permissible, neither in earnest nor in jest; that is because Allah says: {O you who believe, fear Allah and be with the truthful.}"
"1049","1049 - Sa'id narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, from Abu Ma'mar, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: Lying is not permissible, neither in earnest nor in jest, nor that one of you promise his child something and then not fulfill it for him."
"1050","1050 - Sa'id narrated to us, Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, he said: 'Abdullah said: No lying is permissible, neither in earnest nor in jest."
"1051","Verse (122), Allah the Most High's saying: {And it is not for the believers to go forth all together; so why does not a party from every group of them go forth to gain understanding in religion and to warn their people when they return to them, that they may beware?} 1051 - Sa'id narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Ahwal, from 'Ikrimah, he said: I heard him say: When {If you do not go forth, He will punish you with a painful punishment and replace you with a people other than you} was revealed - the hypocrites said: Some people remained who did not go forth, so they are ruined. And there was a people who stayed behind to gain understanding and to warn their people when they returned to them, so the excuse for those was revealed: {So why does not a party from every group of them go forth to gain understanding in religion and to warn their people}, and Allah revealed concerning those [critics]: {And those who dispute concerning Allah after He has been responded to - their argument is invalid with their Lord.}"
"1052","Verse (127), Allah the Most High's saying: {And whenever a surah is revealed, some of them look at one another: Does anyone see you? Then they turn away; Allah has turned away their hearts because they are a people who do not understand.} 1052 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Muslim ibn Subayh, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said: Do not say 'we have turned away (insarafna)'; for a people turned away and Allah turned away their hearts; rather say: We have completed the prayer."
"1053","Verse (128), Allah the Most High's saying: {There has certainly come to you a Messenger from among yourselves; grievous to him is what you suffer, eager for you, to the believers kind and merciful.} 1053 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Yahya ibn Ja'dah, he said: 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) would not confirm a verse in the mushaf until two men testified to it. Then a man of the Ansar came to him and reported to him the two verses at the end of Surah al-Tawbah: {There has certainly come to you} - the verse. He said: I will not ask you for proof for it; such was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - so he confirmed it."
"1054","Verse (129), Allah the Most High's saying: {But if they turn away, say: Allah suffices me; there is no god but He; upon Him I rely, and He is Lord of the Mighty Throne.} 1054 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, he said: He went out intending to hire himself out [as a substitute] in a military expedition that was setting out against him, then in the morning he was preparing, so I said to him: What is the matter with you? Were you not intending to hire yourself out? He said: Yes indeed, but last night I read Surah Bara'ah and heard it urging to jihad."
"1055","Chapter of the Tafsir of Surah Yunus, peace be upon him. Tafsir of Surah Yunus, peace be upon him. Verse (12), Allah the Most High's saying: {And when harm touches man, he calls upon Us lying on his side or sitting or standing; but when We remove from him his harm, he passes on as if he had never called upon Us for harm that touched him.} 1055 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Suqah informed me, he said: I entered with 'Awn ibn 'Abdullah the palace of Kufa, and I said to him: If only you had seen us in the time of al-Hajjaj when we were brought to this palace, with such sorrow and grief upon us! So 'Awn said to me: Then you passed by Him as if you had never called upon Him for harm that touched you! Go to that place and praise Allah, Mighty and Majestic, therein and remember Allah - something like this of speech Sufyan said."
"1056","Verse (16), Allah the Most High's saying: {Say: Had Allah willed, I would not have recited it to you, nor would He have made it known to you.} 1056 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Hanzalah al-Sadusi narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Ibn 'Abbas, that he used to recite (Say: Had Allah willed, I would not have recited it to you, nor would I have warned you of it)."
"1057","Verse (23), Allah the Most High's saying: {But when He saved them, at once they commit injustice upon the earth without right; O mankind, your injustice is only against yourselves.} 1057 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Faraj ibn Fadalah narrated to us, he said: Rabi'ah ibn Yazid narrated to me, from Raja' ibn Haywah, he said: I was in the mosque of Mina when a storyteller was relating, and Raja' said to me: Memorize these words. And there was the storyteller saying: Three traits rebound upon whoever acts by them: plotting, transgression, and breaking [covenants] - Allah said: {O mankind, your transgression is only against yourselves} {And the evil plot does not encompass except its people} {So whoever breaks, he only breaks against himself.} Then he said: O people, three traits - Allah will not punish you as long as you act by them: gratitude to Allah, supplication, and seeking forgiveness. Then he said: {Allah would not punish you if you are grateful and believe} {Say: My Lord would not care for you were it not for your supplication} {And Allah would not punish them while they seek forgiveness.}"
"1058","Verse (26), Allah the Most High's saying: {For those who did good is the best [reward] and increase.} 1058 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Hakam, from 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {For those who did good is the best and increase} - he said: The increase is a chamber of a single pearl having four doors; its chambers and its doors are of a single pearl."
"1059","1059 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit, he said: The increase is looking at the Face of their Lord, Mighty and Majestic."
"1060","1060 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Qabus ibn Abi Zibyan, from his father, from 'Alqamah, he said: He was asked about the increase; he said: The good deed [rewarded] with ten the like of it."
"1061","1061 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: I heard Sufyan say: There is no disagreement in the tafsir of the Qur'an; it is but comprehensive speech intended [to bear] this and that."
"1062","Verse (58), Allah the Most High's saying: {Say: In the bounty of Allah and in His mercy - in that let them rejoice; it is better than what they gather.} 1062 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: al-Ajlah narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: I was commanded to recite the Qur'an to you! He said: I said: Did my Lord name me to you? He said: Yes. Then he recited: {Say: In the bounty of Allah and in His mercy - in that let them rejoice; it is better than what they gather.} He said: By the Book of Allah and by Islam - better than what they gather."
"1063","1063 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas, regarding His saying: {Say: In the bounty of Allah and in His mercy - in that let them rejoice; it is better than what they gather} - he said: By the Book of Allah and by Islam - better than what they gather."
"1064","1064 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated to us, from 'Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: {In the bounty of Allah and in His mercy} - when He made them of His people."
"1065","1065 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak, he said: {In the bounty of Allah} is the Qur'an, {and in His mercy} is Islam."
"1066","Verse (64), Allah the Most High's saying: {For them are glad tidings in the life of this world and in the Hereafter.} 1066 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, he heard 'Ata' ibn Yasar informing from a man of the people of Egypt, he said: I asked Abu al-Darda' about Allah's saying, Mighty and Majestic: {For them are glad tidings in the life of this world.} He said: No one asked me about it before you since I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about it except one man. He said: It is the righteous dream which the Muslim man sees or which is seen for him."
"1067","1067 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from 'Ata' ibn Yasar, from a man of the people of Egypt, from Abu al-Darda', he said: A man asked him about this verse: {For them are glad tidings in the life of this world} - he said: You have asked about something concerning which I never heard anyone ask after a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said to him: It is the righteous dream; the Muslim sees it or it is seen for him - so it is his glad tidings in the life of this world, and his glad tidings in the Hereafter is Paradise."
"1068","1068 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from 'Uthman ibn 'Ubayd al-Rasibi, he said: Abu al-Tufayl 'Amir ibn Wathilah narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no prophethood after me except the mubashshirat. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, and what are the mubashshirat? He said: The righteous dream."
"1069","1069 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Suhaym narrated to me, from Ibrahim ibn 'Abdullah ibn Ma'bad ibn 'Abbas, from his father, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) lifted the curtain while the people were in rows behind Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), and said: Nothing remains of the tidings of prophethood except the righteous dream which the Muslim sees or which is seen for him. Verily I have been forbidden to recite while bowing or prostrating; as for bowing, magnify the Lord therein, and as for prostration, strive in supplication, for it is worthy that it be answered for you."
"1070","Verse (85), Allah the Most High's saying: {So they said: Upon Allah we rely; our Lord, make us not a trial for the wrongdoing people.} 1070 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {Our Lord, make us not a trial for the wrongdoing people} - he said: Do not give them power over us lest they persecute us."
"1071","1071 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, from Tawus, he said: We were with Ibn 'Abbas, and a man of the rulers called al-Hazhāz knelt down and stretched himself tall, until I never saw anyone in the house taller than him. So Ibn 'Abbas said to him: O Hazhāz, do not be a trial for the wrongdoing people! So he shrank until I never saw anyone in the house shorter than him."
"1072","Verse (87), Allah the Most High's saying: {And We inspired to Musa and his brother: Settle your people in Egypt in houses, and make your houses a qiblah.} 1072 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {And make your houses a qiblah} - he said: They would pray only in synagogues (biya'), so it was said to them: Pray in your houses for fear of Pharaoh."
"1073","1073 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: They were afraid, so they were commanded to pray in their houses."
"1074","1074 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, he said: There were people hiding in the time of al-Hajjaj in an upper room to the right of the mosque above a house, and they would pray with the imam the obligatory prayer following him. So I asked Ibrahim about that and he said: It suffices them."
"1075","Verses (88-89), Allah the Most High's saying: {And Musa said: Our Lord, indeed You have given Pharaoh and his chiefs adornment and wealth in the life of this world} up to His saying, the Most High: {He said: Your supplication has been answered, so remain steadfast and do not follow the way of those who do not know.} 1075 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b, he said: {And Musa said: Our Lord, indeed You have given Pharaoh and his chiefs adornment and wealth in the life of this world} up to His saying: {the painful punishment.} Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: {Your supplication has been answered.} He said: Musa would supplicate and Harun would say amin, and the supplicant and the one saying amin are partners."
"1076","Verse (94), Allah the Most High's saying: {So if you are in doubt concerning what We sent down to you, ask those who read the Book before you.} 1076 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, regarding His saying: {So if you are in doubt concerning what We sent down to you, ask those who read the Book before you} - he said: He neither doubted nor asked."
"1077","1077 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, and Mansur, from al-Hasan - they said: He neither doubted nor asked."
"1078","Chapter of the Tafsir of Surah Hud, peace be upon him. Tafsir of Surah Hud, peace be upon him. Verse (5), Allah the Most High's saying: {Verily, they fold their chests to hide from Him; verily, when they cover themselves with their clothes, He knows what they conceal and what they reveal.} 1078 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Husayn, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaddad, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {Verily, they fold their chests to hide from Him} - he said: When one of them passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would fold his chest and cover himself with his garment so that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not see him."
"1079","1079 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn 'Abbas, and Humayd al-A'raj, from Mujahid, that they both used to recite: {Verily, they fold their chests (yathnuna) to hide from Him; verily, when they cover themselves.}"
"1080","Verse (6), Allah the Most High's saying: {And there is no creature upon the earth but upon Allah is its provision, and He knows its dwelling and its repository; all is in a clear Book.} 1080 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {And He knows its dwelling and its repository} - he said: Its dwelling (mustaqarr) is in the womb and in the earth, and its repository (mustawda') is in the loins and in the earth when buried."
"1081","Verse (17), Allah the Most High's saying: {So is one who is upon clear proof from his Lord, and a witness from Him follows him, and before it was the Book of Musa as a guide and mercy - those believe in it; and whoever disbelieves in it of the factions, the Fire is his appointment.} 1081 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, he said: Mujahid used to say regarding His saying: {So is one who is upon clear proof from his Lord, and a witness from Him follows him} - he said: Jibril, peace be upon him; and at-tali means the follower. And he recited: {By the sun and its brightness * And the moon when it follows it.}"
"1082","1082 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {And a witness from Him follows him} - he said: Jibril, may Allah bless him."
"1083","1083 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {So is one who is upon clear proof from his Lord} - he said: Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And a witness from Him follows him - he said: Jibril, peace be upon him."
"1084","1084 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one of this ummah, Jew or Christian, hears of me and does not believe in me except that he shall be of the companions of the Fire. So I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said nothing but what is in the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic - so I read and found it: {And whoever disbelieves in it of the factions, the Fire is his appointment.}"
"1085","Verse (28), Allah the Most High's saying: {So it was made obscure to you; shall we compel you to it while you are averse to it?} 1085 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, he said: Ibn 'Abbas used to say (Shall we compel you to it from part of ourselves while you are averse to it)."
"1086","1086 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu al-'Aliyah, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {So turn your face toward al-Masjid al-Haram} - he said: Toward al-Masjid al-Haram."
"1087","Verse (40), Allah the Most High's saying: {Until when Our command came and the oven gushed forth, We said: Load therein of every [kind] two mates} - the verse. 1087 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from al-'Awwam, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, from Ibn 'Abbas, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {And the oven gushed forth} - he said: Water gushes forth, coming out upon its surface; so it was said to Nuh: When you see the water risen over the earth, then board, you and your companions."
"1088","1088 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from a man - Hushaym said: I think him al-Nu'man ibn Sa'd - from 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), that he said: {And the oven gushed forth} - he said: The rising of the sun."
"1089","Verse (41), Allah the Most High's saying: {And he said: Embark therein; in the name of Allah is its course and its anchorage; indeed my Lord is Forgiving, Merciful.} 1089 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Tamim ibn Salamah, from 'Arfajah, from 'Abdullah, that he used to recite: {Its course (majraha) and its anchorage (mursaha).}"
"1090","Verses (45-46), Allah the Most High's saying: {And Nuh called upon his Lord and said: My Lord, indeed my son is of my household, and indeed Your promise is true, and You are the most just of judges * He said: O Nuh, indeed he is not of your household; indeed it is a deed not righteous} - the verse. 1090 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: I asked Abu Bishr about His saying: {Indeed he is not of your household} - he said: He is not of your household whom I promised you to save with you. Hushaym said: He mentioned it from a man - I do not know whether it is Sa'id ibn Jubayr or someone else."
"1091","1091 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Uthman ibn Matar al-Shaybani narrated to us, he said: Thabit narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Umm Salamah, that she heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite: {A deed not righteous.}"
"1092","1092 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Musa ibn Abi 'A'ishah, from Sulayman ibn Qattah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that he used to recite {Indeed it is a deed not righteous.}"
"1093","1093 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: {A deed not righteous} - your asking Me of what you have no knowledge."
"1094","1094 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Uthman ibn Matar narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said: He was his son, but he differed from him in intention and deed."
"1095","1095 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan and Hushaym narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from al-Sha'bi, he said: 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) went out to pray for rain and did nothing more than seeking forgiveness until he returned. It was said to him: We did not see you pray for rain! He said: I sought rain by the pouring spouts of the heaven by which rain is brought down. Then he recited: {Seek forgiveness of your Lord; indeed He is Forgiving} {He will send the heaven upon you in showers * And O my people, seek forgiveness of your Lord, then repent to Him; He will send the heaven upon you in showers.}"
"1096","Verse (71), Allah the Most High's saying: 1096 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, from Dawud, from al-Sha'bi, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {And after Ishaq, Ya'qub} - he said: From behind a child, a child."
"1097","Verse (80), Allah the Most High's saying: {He said: If only I had against you strength, or could take refuge in a strong support.} 1097 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Mughirah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Hizami narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: May Allah forgive Lut; indeed he was taking refuge in a strong support."
"1098","1098 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Sa'd, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said: Allah did not send a prophet after Lut except amid might of his people."
"1099","Verse (86), Allah the Most High's saying: {What remains with Allah is better for you, if you are believers; and I am not over you a guardian.} 1099 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri', he said: Sufyan was asked about His saying: {What remains with Allah is better for you} - he said: Obedience to Allah is better for you; have you not seen that a man says: O so-and-so, fear Allah, spare yourself."
"1100","Verse (91), Allah the Most High's saying: {They said: O Shu'ayb, we do not understand much of what you say, and indeed we see you among us weak; and were it not for your clan, we would have stoned you; and you are not mighty against us.} 1100 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hudayj ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: Had Lut possessed companions like the companions of Shu'ayb, he would have struggled with them against his people; but there was not among them a right-minded man."
"1101","Verse (100), Allah the Most High's saying: {That is of the news of the towns which We relate to you; of them are standing and harvested.} 1101 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {Of them are standing and harvested} - he said: The standing is what remained of the walls standing, and the harvested is what fell to the ground."
"1102","Verse (114), Allah the Most High's saying: {And establish prayer at the two ends of the day and at the approaches of the night; indeed good deeds remove evil deeds; that is a reminder for the mindful.} 1102 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah - or al-Aswad - from 'Abdullah, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I found a woman in the garden, and I took from her everything except that I did not have intercourse with her, so do with me as you wish! So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was silent toward him. Then the man went away, then he called him and recited to him: {And establish prayer at the two ends of the day and at the approaches of the night; indeed good deeds remove evil deeds; that is a reminder for the mindful.}"
"1103","1103 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid, he heard Ibn 'Abbas deem desirable the delaying of 'Isha and recite: {And at the approaches of the night.}"
"1104","Verses (118-119), Allah the Most High's saying: {And had your Lord willed, He would have made mankind one nation; but they will not cease differing * Except whom your Lord has mercy upon; and for that He created them} - the verse. 1104 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mansur narrated to us, from al-Hasan, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {But they will not cease differing * Except whom your Lord has mercy upon} and likewise {He created them} - he said: He created them for mercy."
"1105","1105 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak, he said: The letter of 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz was read to us: {Except whom your Lord has mercy upon} - he said: The people of mercy do not differ."
"1106","1106 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Uthman ibn Matar narrated to us, he said: Abu Hariz al-Azdi narrated to me, from 'Ikrimah, that he was asked about His saying: {But they will not cease differing * Except whom your Lord has mercy upon; and for that He created them} - he said: He created them for mercy."
"1107","1107 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, he said: Simak narrated to us, from 'Ikrimah, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {But they will not cease differing * Except whom your Lord has mercy upon} - he said: Differing in desires."
"1108","Verse (120), Allah the Most High's saying: {And all We relate to you of the news of the messengers is that by which We make firm your heart; and there has come to you in this the truth, and admonition and reminder for the believers.} 1108 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from 'Amr - a man of Bal'anbar - he said: Ibn 'Abbas gave a sermon and recited Hud; then when he reached: {And there has come to you in this the truth} - he said: In this surah."
"1109","1109 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Yahya al-Abahh narrated to us, he said: Yazid al-Raqashi narrated to us, from Anas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: His companions said to him: Gray hair has come quickly upon you! He said: Hud and its sisters of the Mufassal have grayed me."
"1110","1110 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from 'Ikrimah, he said: Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Messenger of Allah, what has grayed you? He said: Hud, al-Waqi'ah, al-Mursalat, 'Amma yatasa'alun, and Idha al-shamsu kuwwirat have grayed me."
"1111","Chapter of the Tafsir of Surah Yusuf, peace be upon him. Tafsir of Surah Yusuf, peace be upon him. Verse (4) - Allah the Most High's saying: {When Yusuf said to his father: O my father, indeed I saw eleven stars, and the sun and the moon; I saw them prostrating to me.} 1111 - Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit al-Qurashi, from Jabir ibn 'Abdullah, he said: There came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a man called Bustani the Jew, and he said: O Muhammad, inform me of the stars which Yusuf saw prostrating to him; what are their names? He said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not answer him with anything, then Jibril, peace be upon him, descended to him and informed him. So the Prophet of Allah sent for the Jew and he came to him. He said: What do you think - will you submit if I inform you? He said: Yes. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Hurthan, al-Tariq, al-Dhayyal, Dhu al-Kanafat, Dhu al-Fara', Waththab, 'Amudan, Qabis, al-Saruh, al-Musabbih, al-Faliq, al-Diya' and al-Nur - he saw them in the horizon of the heaven prostrating to him. When Yusuf related his dream to Ya'qub, he said to him: This is a scattered matter which Allah will gather thereafter. The Jew said: By Allah, these are their names. Al-Hakam said: Al-Diya' is the sun, and it is his father; and al-Nur is the moon, and it is his mother."
"1112","Verse (20), Allah the Most High's saying: {And they sold him for a cheap price - a few dirhams - and they were of those who abstain regarding him.} 1112 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Khalid, he said: I heard al-Suddi swear that what they bought him for was twenty-two dirhams; and Sufyan said: Al-bakhs is the unlawful."
"1113","Verse (21), Allah the Most High's saying: {And the one who bought him in Egypt said to his wife: Honor his stay; perhaps he will benefit us or we will take him as a son} - the verse. 1113 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: People of the companions of 'Abdullah narrated to us; they said: 'Abdullah said: Of the most discerning of people are three: al-'Aziz who bought Yusuf, when he said: {Perhaps he will benefit us or we will take him as a son.} And the woman who said to her father concerning Musa: {O my father, hire him; indeed the best you can hire is the strong, the trustworthy.} And Abu Bakr when he entrusted to 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) the affairs of the Muslims."
"1114","Verse (23), Allah the Most High's saying: {And she in whose house he was sought to seduce him, and she bolted the doors and said: Come to me.} 1114 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Yahya ibn Waththab, that he used to recite (huyyi'tu laka - I have been prepared for you)."
"1115","Verse (24), Allah the Most High's saying: {And she certainly inclined to him, and he would have inclined to her had he not seen the proof of his Lord; thus that We avert from him evil and immorality; indeed he is of Our sincere servants.} 1115 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hassan ibn Ibrahim al-Kirmani narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from al-Zuhri, he said: Humayd ibn 'Abd al-Rahman informed me that the proof which Yusuf saw was Ya'qub."
"1116","1116 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Uthman ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn 'Abbas, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {Had he not seen the proof of his Lord} - he said: He loosened the waist-wrapper and sat with her in the position of the circumciser, then he was called out: Will you commit adultery, O son of Ya'qub, and become like a bird that tried to fly and its feathers fell off?"
"1117","1117 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid, he heard Ibn 'Abbas being asked: What did the inclination of Yusuf reach? He said: He loosened the waist-wrapper and sat with her in the position of the circumciser."
"1118","1118 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mis'ar, from one who narrated to him, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: He saw Ya'qub biting upon his hands, and his desire exited from his fingertips."
"1119","1119 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, he said: He saw the image of Ya'qub."
"1120","1120 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, he said: He saw the image of Ya'qub biting upon his finger."
"1121","1121 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mughirah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, he said: When Yusuf sat with her in that sitting and loosened the trousers until they reached the thighs - Ya'qub appeared to him and struck his chest with his hand, saying: O Yusuf! So his desire exited from his fingertips."
"1122","Verse (30), Allah the Most High's saying: {And women in the city said: The wife of al-'Aziz seeks to seduce her slave boy; he has smitten her with love; indeed we see her in clear error.} 1122 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, that he used to recite: {He has smitten her (shaghafaha) with love} and would say: Al-shaghaf is the smiting of love, and al-sha'af is the fright of a beast when startled."
"1123","1123 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, and 'Awf, from Ibrahim, that they both recited: {Shaghafaha.}"
"1124","Verse (36), Allah the Most High's saying: {And there entered with him into the prison two youths} up to His saying, the Most High: {Indeed we see you of the doers of good.} 1124 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, he said: Salamah ibn Nubayt narrated to us, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, he said: We were with him in Khurasan, and a man asked him about His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {Inform us of its interpretation; indeed we see you of the doers of good} - what was the goodness of Yusuf? Al-Dahhak said: When a man fell ill he would attend to him, when one was straitened he would make room for him, and when one was in need he would collect for him."
"1125","Verse (42), Allah the Most High's saying: {And he said to the one whom he thought would be saved of the two: Mention me with your lord; but Satan made him forget the mention of his lord, so he remained in prison some years.} 1125 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, in the reading of 'Abdullah: {Some (bid') years} - near [in number]."
"1126","Verse (45), Allah the Most High's saying: {And the one who was saved of the two, and remembered after a while, said: I will inform you of its interpretation, so send me.} 1126 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak, that he used to recite: (And remembered after forgetfulness - ba'da amh) i.e. after forgetfulness."
"1127","Verse (49), Allah the Most High's saying: {Then there will come after that a year in which the people will be given rain and in which they will press.} 1127 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Faraj ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talhah, from Ibn 'Abbas, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {And in which they will press (ya'sirun)} - they will milk."
"1128","Verses (52-53), Allah the Most High's saying: {That, that he may know I did not betray him in absence, and that Allah does not guide the plot of the betrayers * And I do not absolve myself; indeed the soul commands to evil.} 1128 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, from Bayan, from Hakim ibn Jabir, he said: Yusuf said {That, that he may know I did not betray him in absence.} He said: I was told that Jibril said to him: Not even when you inclined? He said: {And I do not absolve myself; indeed the soul commands to evil.}"
"1129","Verse (54), Allah the Most High's saying: {And the king said: Bring him to me; I will take him exclusively for myself. So when he spoke to him, he said: Indeed you are today with us established, trusted.} 1129 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hibban ibn 'Ali narrated to us, from Abu Sinan Dirar ibn Murrah, from 'Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, he said: Al-'Aziz said to Yusuf: There is nothing except that I love you to share me in it, except that I do not love you to share me in my wife! Yusuf said: Nor I. And I do not love that my servant eat with me! Yusuf said: Do you disdain me while I am the son of Ishaq the sacrificed, and I am the son of Ya'qub the prophet of Allah?!"
"1130","Verse (62), Allah the Most High's saying: {And he said to his servants: Put their goods in their saddlebags, that they may recognize them when they return to their people, that they may return.} 1130 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, that he used to recite: {And he said to his lads (li-fityatihi).}"
"1131","1131 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from 'Awf and 'Abbad ibn Rashid, from al-Hasan, that he used to recite: {To his servants (li-fityanihi).}"
"1132","Verse (65), Allah the Most High's saying: {And when they opened their goods, they found their goods returned to them; they said: O our father, what do we seek? These are our goods returned to us.} 1132 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah, that he used to recite {These are our goods returned to us.}"
"1133","Verse (67), Allah the Most High's saying: {And he said: O my sons, do not enter by one gate, but enter by different gates; and I avail you nothing against Allah; judgment is only Allah's; upon Him I rely, and upon Him let the reliant rely.} 1133 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, he said: A man of the people of Kufa narrated to us, from Ibrahim, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {Do not enter by one gate, but enter by different gates} up to His saying: {Let the reliant rely} - he said: Ya'qub loved that the brothers of Yusuf meet Yusuf in private."
"1134","Verse (72), Allah the Most High's saying: {They said: We miss the king's cup, and for whoever brings it is a camel-load, and I am its guarantor.} 1134 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, regarding His saying: {The king's cup (suwa')} - he said: It is the Persian makkuk (measure) whose two ends meet; the non-Arabs used to drink in it."
"1135","1135 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, that he used to recite: {The king's cup (suwa')} - he said: His vessel in which he used to drink."
"1136","1136 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-'Abbas ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, that he used to recite (the king's sa' - sa'a al-malik)."
"1137","Verse (76), Allah the Most High's saying: {We raise in degrees whom We will, and above every possessor of knowledge is a Knower.} 1137 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from 'Abd al-A'la, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {And above every possessor of knowledge is a Knower} - he said: Allah, the All-Knowing, the All-Aware, is above every learned one."
"1138","Verse (86), Allah the Most High's saying: {He said: I only complain of my grief and sorrow to Allah, and I know from Allah what you do not know.} 1138 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd, he heard 'Abdullah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had say: I heard the sobbing of 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) while I was in the last rows: {I only complain of my grief and sorrow to Allah.}"
"1139","Verse (88), Allah the Most High's saying: {So when they entered upon him, they said: O mighty one, hardship has touched us and our family, and we have come with scant goods; so give us full measure and be charitable to us; indeed Allah rewards the charitable.} 1139 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Masruq narrated to us, from 'Ikrimah, regarding His saying: {And we have come with scant goods (muzjah)} - i.e. little."
"1140","1140 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn al-Harith, he said: Little - the goods of the Bedouins: wool and ghee."
"1141","1141 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Uthman ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that he was asked about the scant goods; he said: Worn-out sacks, ropes, vessels, and things."
"1142","1142 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir informed me, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman al-Tawil narrated to me that a man said to 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz: Be charitable to me - may Allah be charitable to you with Paradise! He said: Allah does not give charity, but He rewards the charitable."
"1143","1143 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: 'Uthman ibn al-Aswad informed me, from Mujahid, he said: Do not say 'be charitable to me' - only one who seeks reward gives charity."
"1144","Verse (98), Allah the Most High's saying: {He said: I shall seek forgiveness for you from my Lord; indeed He is the Forgiving, the Merciful.} 1144 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from his uncle, he said: I used to pass by the house of 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud and hear him say: O Allah, You called me and I answered, and You commanded me and I obeyed, and this is the pre-dawn, so forgive me. Then I met him and said: Words I heard you say at pre-dawn - and I informed him of them. He said: Ya'qub deferred his sons to the pre-dawn."
"1145","Verse (101), Allah the Most High's saying: {My Lord, You have given me of sovereignty and taught me of the interpretation of narratives; Originator of the heavens and the earth, You are my guardian in this world and the Hereafter; cause me to die a Muslim and join me with the righteous.} 1145 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: I heard Sufyan recite this verse: {My Lord, You have given me of sovereignty and taught me of the interpretation of narratives; Originator of the heavens and the earth, You are my guardian in this world and the Hereafter; cause me to die a Muslim} - he said: No one asked it before him; when his parents were gathered to him and he rejoiced, he asked his Lord to cause him to die and join him with the righteous."
"1146","Verse (106), Allah the Most High's saying: {And most of them do not believe in Allah except while they associate.} 1146 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from 'Ata', regarding His saying: {And most of them do not believe in Allah except while they associate} - he said: They knew that Allah is their Lord, and He is their Creator, and He is their Provider; and along with that they associated."
"1147","Verse (110), Allah the Most High's saying: {Until when the messengers despaired and thought that they had been denied, there came to them Our help, so whoever We will was saved} - the verse. 1147 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, from Husayn, from 'Imran ibn al-Harith, from Ibn 'Abbas, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {Until when the messengers despaired and thought that they had been denied} - he said: The messengers despaired of their people responding to them, and the people thought that the messengers had been lied to - then the command of Allah came."
"1148","1148 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, he said: 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: The messengers despaired of their people believing, and their people thought that the messengers had been lied to - then Our help came to them, so whoever We will is saved."
"1149","1149 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Husayn, from 'Imran ibn al-Harith, from Ibn 'Abbas, that he used to recite: {And thought that they had been denied (kudhdhibu)} - light (with takhfif, passive)."
"1150","1150 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from Tamim ibn Hadlam, from Ibn Mas'ud, that he used to recite: {And thought that they had been denied (kudhdhibu)} - light (with takhfif, passive)."
"1151","1151 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Muslim ibn Subayh, from Ibn 'Abbas, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {Until when the messengers despaired and thought that they had been denied} - he said: When the messengers despaired that their people would respond to them, and their people thought that the messengers had lied to them - help came upon that, so whoever We will was saved."
"1152","1152 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah, he said: 'Abdullah said: I recited Surah Yusuf in Hims, and a man said: It was not revealed thus. So I drew near him and found the smell of wine from him. I said to him: Do you deny the truth and drink filth! By Allah, thus did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) teach it to me; by Allah, I will not leave you until I flog you the hadd! He said: So he flogged him the hadd."
"1153","Chapter 50, Tafsir of Surah al-Ra'd. Tafsir of Surah al-Ra'd. Verse (4), Allah the Most High's saying: {And in the earth are neighboring tracts, and gardens of grapevines, and crops, and date-palms, clustered and not clustered, watered with one water} - the verse. 1153 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hudayj ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara' ibn 'Azib, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {Clustered and not clustered} - he said: Al-sinwan is that its root be one and its tops separate, and ghayr sinwan is that the palm be solitary with nothing near it."
"1154","Verse (8), Allah the Most High's saying: {Allah knows what every female carries, and what the wombs diminish and what they increase; and everything with Him is by measure.} 1154 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Abu Bishr narrated to us, from Mujahid, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {He knows what every female carries, and what the wombs diminish and what they increase} - he said: What exceeds the nine months is the increase, and it is completion for that diminution."
"1155","1155 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Mujahid, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {And what the wombs diminish and what they increase} - he said: When the woman menstruates upon her child it is a diminution in the child; then when she exceeds nine months it is completion for what was diminished of it."
"1156","1156 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Attab ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: The number of every day that increases while she is pregnant becomes an addition in the term of pregnancy."
"1157","1157 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from 'Asim al-Ahwal, from 'Ikrimah, he said: Al-ghayd is menstruation during pregnancy; for every day she menstruates in her pregnancy, a day is added in her pregnancy until she completes the pregnancy in purity."
"1158","1158 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Yahya, from al-Dahhak, he said: Al-ghayd is what is less than nine [months], and what increases is what is more than nine."
"1159","Verse (11), Allah the Most High's saying: {For him are successive [angels] before him and behind him, guarding him by the command of Allah} - the verse. 1159 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, he said: Ibn 'Abbas used to recite: For him are successive [angels] before him, and watchers behind him, guarding him by the command of Allah."
"1160","1160 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Rib'i ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-Jarud ibn Abi Sabrah narrated to us, he said: al-Jarud ibn Abi Sabrah narrated to me, he said: I entered with my father upon Ibn 'Abbas in Sham on a Friday, and he had come out of his bath - having taken ghusl, while I was reclining - reciting: {For him are successive [angels] before him and behind him, guarding him by the command of Allah.} So Ibn 'Abbas said: O Abu Sabrah, the mu'aqqibat are not there; rather: For him are successive [angels] behind him, and a watcher before him."
"1161","Verse (13), His saying, Exalted is He: {And the thunder glorifies with His praise, and the angels out of fear of Him, and He sends thunderbolts and strikes with them whom He wills, while they dispute about Allah, and He is severe in assault} - 1161 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Salim narrated to us, from Abu Salih, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {And the thunder glorifies with His praise} - he said: Thunder is an angel among the angels who glorifies."
"1162","1162 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Abi al-Walid narrated to us, from Ziyad al-Ju'fi, from Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ali, he said: Thunderbolts strike the Muslim and the non-Muslim, but they do not strike one who remembers Allah."
"1163","1163 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Salim narrated to us, from al-Hakam, he said: There descend with the rain more angels than the children of Adam and the children of Iblis."
"1164","1164 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us, from Ghaylan ibn Jarir, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Whoever hears the sound of thunder, let him say: Glory be to the One whom you have glorified, glory be to Allah the Tremendous - twice."
"1165","1165 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sallam al-Tawil narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Fulan, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Whoever hears the sound of thunder and says: Glory be to the One whom the thunder glorifies with His praise, and the angels out of fear of Him, and He is over all things Powerful - then if a thunderbolt strikes him, his blood-money is upon me."
"1166","Verse (18), His saying, Exalted is He: {For those who responded to their Lord is the best reward, and those who did not respond to Him, if they had...} up to His saying: {Those will have an evil reckoning, and their abode is Hell, and wretched is the resting place} - 1166 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Awn ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: I heard Farqad al-Sabakhi saying: An evil reckoning is that nothing of it is overlooked for him."
"1167","1167 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from a man, from Ibrahim, he said: An evil reckoning is that He seizes His servant with exact justice."
"1168","Verse (23), His saying, Exalted is He: {Gardens of Eden which they will enter, along with the righteous among their fathers, their spouses and their offspring} - 1168 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Awn ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan saying: Gardens of Eden - and what do you know what Gardens of Eden are! A palace of gold, which none shall enter except a prophet, or a truthful one, or a martyr, or a just ruler."
"1169","Verse (28), His saying, Exalted is He: {Those who believed and whose hearts find rest in the remembrance of Allah; indeed, in the remembrance of Allah do hearts find rest} - 1169 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {Those who believed and whose hearts find rest in the remembrance of Allah} - he said: They are the Companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1170","Verse (29), His saying, Exalted is He: {Those who believed and did righteous deeds, blessedness is for them and a good return} - 1170 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Hassan ibn Abi al-Ashras, from Mughith ibn Sumayy, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {Blessedness is for them and a good return} - he said: A tree in Paradise, there is no household but a branch of its branches shades them; in it are fruits of all colours, and birds like Bactrian camels alight upon it; when a man desires a bird he calls it until it lands on his tray, and he eats from one side of it roasted and the other side dried meat, then it flies away."
"1171","1171 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Humayd al-A'raj, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: You will look at a bird and desire it, and it will fall before you roasted, and you will eat from it."
"1172","Verse (31), His saying, Exalted is He: {And if there were a Qur'an by which the mountains were moved, or the earth cut apart, or the dead spoken to; rather, to Allah belongs the affair entirely. Did those who believed not despair that if Allah willed He would have guided all people? And those who disbelieved will not cease to be struck by a calamity for what they did, or it alights near their home, until the promise of Allah comes; indeed Allah does not break the promise} - 1172 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Hanzalah al-Sadusi, he said: I recited before Ikrimah 'Did those who disbelieved not despair', so he said: Rather it is: 'Let those who believed know'. He said: So I mentioned that to Shahr ibn Hawshab and he said: He spoke the truth; Ibn Abbas corrected him on it."
"1173","1173 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, regarding His saying: {And those who disbelieved will not cease to be struck by a calamity for what they did, or it alights near their home} - he said: You will alight near their home."
"1174","Verse (41), His saying, Exalted is He: {Have they not seen that We come to the land reducing it from its borders? And Allah judges; there is no repeller of His judgment, and He is swift in reckoning} - 1174 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {Have they not seen that We come to the land reducing it from its borders} - he said: The reduction."
"1175","1175 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, Juwaybir narrated to us, from al-Dahhak, he said: Have they not seen that We open for Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) land after land? Are they the victors? Rather, Allah and His Messenger are the victors."
"1176","1176 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Husayn, from Abu Malik, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {Have they not seen that We come to the land reducing it from its borders} - he said: A town, one of its sides falls into ruin."
"1177","Verse (43), His saying, Exalted is He: {And those who disbelieved say: You are not sent. Say: Sufficient is Allah as a witness between me and you, and whoever has knowledge of the Book} - 1177 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, he said: I asked Sa'id ibn Jubayr about His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {and whoever has knowledge of the Book} - is it Abdullah ibn Salam? He said: How could it be, when this surah is Makkan? And Sa'id ibn Jubayr used to recite: (and from Him is the knowledge of the Book)."
"1178","In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. [My Lord, make easy by Your mercy, O Generous One]. The shaykh, the memorizer Abu al-Barakat Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Mubarak ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Anmati informed us, he said: The trustworthy Abu Tahir Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Baqillani al-Karkhi, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us, he said: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Shadhan informed us, recited to him while I listened, he said: Abu Muhammad Da'laj ibn Ahmad ibn Da'laj al-Sijistani informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Zayd al-Sa'igh informed us, he said: Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Chapter on encouragement to teach the shares of inheritance. 1 - Abu Awanah, Abu al-Ahwas and Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Muwarriq al-Ijli, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Learn the shares of inheritance, the mispronunciations, and the Sunnah, just as you learn the Qur'an."
"1179","2 - Sa'id said: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid and Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, he said: Umar said: Learn the shares of inheritance, for they are part of your religion."
"1180","3 - Sa'id said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq informed us, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, he said: Whoever learns the Qur'an, let him learn the shares of inheritance."
"1181","4 - Sa'id said: Muhammad ibn Thabit al-Abdi narrated to us, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most merciful of my community to my community is Abu Bakr, and the sternest and most delicate of them in the matter of Allah is Umar, and the most modest of them is Uthman, and the most knowledgeable of them in the lawful and unlawful is Mu'adh ibn Jabal, and the most knowledgeable of them in inheritance shares is Zayd ibn Thabit, and the best reciter of them is Ubayy ibn Ka'b. And it was said: The most knowledgeable of them in judiciary is Ali."
"1182","Chapter on the foundations of the shares of inheritance. 5 - Sa'id said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Kharijah ibn Zayd ibn Thabit: The meanings of all these inheritance shares and their foundations are from Zayd ibn Thabit, and Abu al-Zinad explained them according to the meanings of Zayd ibn Thabit. (a) A man inherits from his wife - if she left no child and no son's child - half; if she left a child or a son's child, male or female, her husband inherits a fourth, with nothing reduced from that; and a woman inherits from her husband, if he left no child and no son's child, a fourth; if he left a child or a son's child, his wife inherits an eighth. (b) The inheritance of the mother from her child - if her son or daughter died leaving a child or a son's child, male or female, or leaving two or more siblings, male or female, full or paternal or maternal - is a sixth; if the deceased left no child, no son's child, and no two or more siblings, then the mother gets a full third, except in two cases: a man dies leaving his wife and his two parents, so his wife gets a fourth, the mother gets a third of what remains, which is a fourth of the whole estate; and a woman dies leaving her husband and her two parents, so the husband gets half, her mother gets a third of what remains, which is a sixth of the whole estate. (c) The inheritance of the maternal siblings: they inherit nothing with a child, nor with a son's child male or female, nor with the father, nor with the grandfather, the father's father; in all other cases a single one of them, male or female, is assigned a sixth, and if they are two or more, male or female, a third is assigned to them, which they share equally, male like female. (d) The inheritance of the father from his son or daughter when deceased: if the deceased left a male child or a male son's child, a sixth is assigned to the father; if the deceased left no male child and no male son's child, then the father is made residuary: those who share with him among the fixed-sharers are begun with and given their shares, and if a sixth or more of the wealth remains it is for the father, but if less than a sixth remains, a sixth is assigned to the father as a fixed share. (e) The inheritance of children from their father or mother: if a man or woman died leaving one daughter, she gets half; if there are two or more females, they get two-thirds; if there is a male with them, then none of them has a fixed share: whoever shares with them with a fixed share is begun with and given his share, and what remains after that is for the children among them, for the male the like of the share of two females. (f) The inheritance of the sons' children, when there is no child below them, is exactly like the standing of children: their males like their males and their females like their females; they inherit as they inherit and are excluded as they are excluded; if children and son's children combine, and there is a male among the children, then none of the son's children inherits with him; if there is no male among the children and there are two or more daughters, then the son's daughters inherit nothing with them unless there is with the son's daughters a male who is at their level relative to the deceased or further removed, in which case any remainder is returned upon those at his level and those above him among the son's daughters, and they divide it, for the male the like of the share of two females; if nothing remains, they get nothing; if the children are only one daughter and he left a son's daughter, or more son's daughters at one level, they get a sixth completing the two-thirds; if there is with the son's daughters a male at their level, they get no sixth and no fixed share, but if anything remains after the fixed-sharers' shares, that remainder is for that male and the females at his level, for the male the like of the share of two females, and those further removed than them get nothing; if nothing remains, they get nothing. (g) The inheritance of the full brothers: they inherit nothing with a male child, nor with a male son's child, nor with the father; with daughters and son's daughters, so long as the deceased did not leave a grandfather, the father's father, they become residuaries: whoever has a fixed share is begun with and they are given their shares, and if anything remains after that it is for the full brothers among them according to the Book of Allah, whether female or male, for the male the like of the share of two females; if nothing remains, they get nothing; if the deceased left no father, no grandfather who is the father's father, no child and no son's child male or female, then a single full sister is assigned half, and if there are two or more sisters they are assigned two-thirds; if there is a male brother with them, then none of the sisters has a fixed share: those who share with them among the fixed-sharers are begun with and given their shares, and what remains after that is among the full brothers, for the male the like of the share of two females, except in one single case in which nothing remained for them, so they were shared with their maternal siblings: a woman died leaving her husband, her mother, her maternal siblings and her full siblings, so her husband got half, her mother a sixth, her maternal siblings a third, and nothing remained, so the full siblings are shared in this case with the maternal siblings in their third, for the male the like of the share of two females, because they were all children of the deceased's mother. (h) The inheritance of the paternal brothers, when there is none of the full siblings with them, is exactly like the inheritance of the full siblings: their males like their males and their females like their females, except that they are not shared with the maternal siblings in the case in which the full siblings shared with them; if full siblings and paternal siblings combine and there is a male among the full siblings, then none of the paternal siblings inherits with him; if the full siblings are only one woman and the paternal siblings are one woman or more females with no male among them, then half is assigned to the full sister and a sixth completing the two-thirds is assigned to the paternal sisters; if there is a male with the paternal daughters, they have no fixed share: the fixed-sharers are begun with and given their shares, and if anything remains after that it is among the paternal siblings, for the male the like of the share of two females; if nothing remains for them, they get nothing; if the full siblings are two or more females, they are assigned two-thirds and the paternal daughters inherit nothing with them unless there is with them a male from the father: if there is a male with them, the fixed shares of whoever has a fixed share are begun with and given, and if anything remains after that it is among the paternal siblings, for the male the like of the share of two females; if nothing remains for them, they get nothing. (i) The inheritance of the grandfather, the father's father: he inherits nothing with a nearer father; with a male child and with a son's son, a sixth is assigned to him; in all other cases, so long as the deceased did not leave a brother or sister from his father, the grandfather is made residuary: whoever shares with him among the fixed-sharers is begun with and given his share, and if a sixth or more of the wealth remains it is for the grandfather, but if less than a sixth remains, a sixth is assigned to the grandfather as a fixed share. (j) The inheritance of the grandfather, the father's father, with full siblings: they become residuaries, and whoever shares with them among the fixed-sharers is begun with and they are given their shares; whatever remains for the grandfather and the siblings is then looked into and calculated as to which is better for the grandfather's share: a third of what accrues to him and the siblings, or to be as a brother sharing with the siblings in what accrues to them and him, for the male the like of the share of two females, or a sixth of the whole capital outright; whichever of these is better for the grandfather's share, the grandfather is given it, and what remains after that is among the full brothers, except in one single case in which their division is otherwise. (al-Akdariyyah): it is a woman who died leaving her husband, her mother, her grandfather and her paternal sister: half is assigned to the husband, a third to the mother, a sixth to the grandfather and half to the sister; then the grandfather's sixth and the sister's half are gathered and divided entirely into thirds: two-thirds of it for the grandfather and a third for the sister. (ja) The inheritance of the paternal brothers with the grandfather, when there are no full siblings with them, is exactly like the inheritance of the full siblings: their males like their males and their females like their females; if full siblings and paternal siblings combine, then the full siblings reckon against the grandfather with their paternal siblings, withholding by them much of the inheritance from him; whatever accrues to the siblings after the grandfather's share is for the full siblings and not for the paternal siblings, unless the full siblings are only one woman: if she is one woman, she reckons against the grandfather with her paternal siblings, whatever they may be, and whatever accrues to her and them is hers to their exclusion up to her completing half of the wealth; if in what is set aside for her and them there is an excess over half of the whole wealth, that excess is among the paternal siblings, for the male the like of the share of two females; if nothing remains, they get nothing. (jb) The inheritance of the grandmothers: the mother's mother inherits nothing with the mother, and in all other cases a sixth is assigned to her as a fixed share; the father's mother inherits nothing with the mother nor with the father, and in all other cases a sixth is assigned to her as a fixed share; if the deceased left three grandmothers at one level, with no mother or father below them, then a sixth is among the three of them: the mother's mother's mother, the mother's father's mother, and the father's father's mother. (jc) Abu al-Zinad said: If two grandmothers combine, with no father or mother of the deceased below them, then we have heard that if the one from the mother's side is the nearer of the two, she gets the sixth to the exclusion of the one from the father's side; but if they are at one level relative to the deceased, or the one from the father's side is the nearer, the sixth is between them in halves."
"1183","6 - Sa'id said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, he said: Mansur informed us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, he said: Abdullah said: Whenever Umar ibn al-Khattab took us along a path and we followed him, we found it easy; and he was asked about a wife and two parents, so he said: For the wife a fourth, for the mother a third of what remains, and what remains is for the father."
"1184","7 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash informed us, he said: Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Mas'ud said: Umar, when he took us along a path and we followed it, we found it easy; and he was approached regarding a wife and two parents, and he made it from four shares: for the wife a fourth, for the mother a third of what remains, and for the father what remains, which is two shares."
"1185","8 - Sa'id said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah was approached regarding a wife and two parents, so he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, when he took us along a path we followed it; and he was approached regarding a wife and two parents, and he made it from four shares: he gave the wife a fourth, gave the mother a third of what remains, and gave the father the rest of that."
"1186","9 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Khalid informed us, from Abu Qilabah, that Uthman ibn Affan was approached regarding a wife and two parents, and he made it from four."
"1187","10 - Sa'id said: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Khalid, from Abu Qilabah, from Uthman ibn Affan regarding a wife and two parents: he gave the wife a fourth, one share, gave the mother a third of what remains, one share, and gave the father what remains, two shares."
"1188","11 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Khalid informed us, from Abu Qilabah, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that he said regarding a husband and two parents: he made it from six: for the husband three shares, for the mother a third of what remains, one share, and what remains is for the father, two shares."
"1189","12 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Layla informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Abdullah and Zayd ibn Thabit, the like of that."
"1190","13 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Hajjaj ibn Artah, he said: A shaykh from Hamdan narrated to us, from al-Harith, from Ali, that he said regarding a husband and two parents: he gave the husband half, three shares, for the mother a third of what remains, and for the father two shares."
"1191","14 - Sa'id said: Abu Shihab narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from one who heard Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ali, from his father, from Ali, that he said: Regarding a husband and two parents, for the husband is half, and for the mother a third of what remains."
"1192","15 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Layla informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that Ali said: For the mother is a third of what remains."
"1193","16 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from one of his companions, from Ali, that he used to say: For the mother is a third of the whole estate."
"1194","17 - Sa'id said: Abu Shihab narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Umayr ibn Sa'id, he said: al-Harith al-A'war taught me regarding a husband and two parents: for the husband half, and for the mother a third of what remains."
"1195","18 - Sa'id said: Abu Shihab narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Muslim ibn Subayh, from Masruq ibn al-Ajda', he said: Ibn Mas'ud used to say regarding full sisters and paternal brothers and sisters: for the full sisters two-thirds, and the rest of the wealth is for the males to the exclusion of the females; then when Masruq came to Madinah and heard the opinion of Zayd ibn Thabit on it, it pleased him, so one of his companions said to him: Do you abandon the opinion of Abdullah? He said: I came to Madinah and found Zayd ibn Thabit among those firmly grounded in knowledge."
"1196","19 - Sa'id said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Masruq, he said: He used to follow the opinion of Abdullah regarding full sisters, giving what remains of the two-thirds to the males to the exclusion of the females; then he went on a journey to Madinah, and came back holding that they should be shared among them, so Alqamah said to him: What turned you away from the opinion of Abdullah? Did you meet someone more established in your view than him? He said: No, but I met Zayd ibn Thabit and found him among those firmly grounded in knowledge."
"1197","Chapter of al-Musharraka. 20 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, that Umar, Ibn Mas'ud and Zayd ibn Thabit said: In al-Musharraka, for the husband is half, for the mother a sixth, and what remains, which is a third, the full brothers and sisters and the maternal brothers and sisters are shared in it, male and female being equal in it."
"1198","21 - Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, he said: Umar, Ibn Mas'ud and Zayd ibn Thabit used to share among them, while Ali did not share."
"1199","22 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, from Abu Mijlaz, from Ali that he gave the husband half, the mother a sixth, and the remaining third to the maternal brothers, and he excluded the full brothers and sisters; and that Uthman ibn Affan shared among them."
"1200","23 - Sa'id said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Layla informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that Umar and Ibn Mas'ud shared among them."
